{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MXQqw7bvqPoP2FsCX4NLSm","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: agentic-sdlc-factory\n3\tdescription: \"Ongoing design of a self-improving multi-agent SDLC \\\"factory\\\" at ~/Projects/agentic-sdlc\"\n4\tmetadata: \n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: 800a79a5-f568-48d8-aee9-a453e54892c9\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\tThe user is designing a **self-improving SDLC \"factory\"** — a deterministic multi-agent workflow\n11\tthat builds apps (planner → PRD/TRD → TDD build loop → adversarial review → PO sign-off) and then\n12\taudits *how it built* the feature to auto-improve its own agents/prompts/skills/hooks.\n13\t\n14\tLives at `~/Projects/agentic-sdlc/` (NOT a git repo yet). Full design in `ARCHITECTURE.md`.\n15\tKey decisions already made (see §11 decisions log there before re-deriving):\n16\t- **Factory ⇄ products** separation; every learning has a **scope** (app-specific / archetype /\n17\t  factory-general) = \"planes\" projected onto each lever (skill/hook/prompt/agent/workflow).\n18\t- **Two-tier eval:** per-agent **auditor** (objective, observe-not-prescribe, always-on) →\n19\t  **synthesizer** (correlates, classifies scope+blast-radius, emits auto-applied changeset).\n20\t- **Guardrails:** commit every change (revertible); blast-radius tiering; protective agents (PO,\n21\t  adversarial) never tuned toward leniency (\"don't silence your critics\"); synthesizer reads the\n22\t  corpus not a single run.\n23\t- Improvements **auto-apply** (no human review) — user's explicit choice; recoverability via\n24\t  commits substitutes for review.\n25\t\n26\tArtifacts done: `charters/*.md` (7 role rubrics), `schema/run-record.schema.json`,\n27\t`apps/_TEMPLATE/profile.md`, `gates.md` (definition-of-done + verdict schema per step — the\n28\tcontrol-flow contract, distinct from charter rubrics), and the two workflow scripts\n29\t`workflows/build-loop.mjs` + `workflows/eval-loop.mjs` (drafted, not yet run). First app chosen:\n30\t**pinewood-derby-sim** (frontend; TS/React/Vitest; teaches kids derby physics; educational\n31\taccuracy is a hard requirement) at `apps/pinewood-derby-sim/profile.md`.\n32\t\n33\tDecisions: v1 builds work items **sequentially** (shared codebase; parallel-worktree is later).\n34\t**First app is Python 3.12 via uv** (pytest/ruff/mypy; NO Node anywhere; `uv run <cmd>` is the\n35\tcommand pattern in the profile) — engine-first, pure physics engine, pygame UI deferred; archetype\n36\t`desktop-app`.\n37\t\n38\tDONE: 7 agent defs in `agentic-sdlc/.claude/agents/` (wrap charters; tools scoped — auditor/\n39\tsynthesizer read-only). `git init` + baseline commit done. Python venv + tooling installed and all\n40\t3 gate commands verified passing on the scaffold. Agent discovery wired via symlink\n41\t`~/Projects/.claude/agents → agentic-sdlc/.claude/agents` — **UNVERIFIED until a workflow runs**\n42\t(cwd project root is ~/Projects, not the factory).\n43\t\n44\tDONE (2026-06-02): first real **build-loop** run of `0001-physics-engine` completed and\n45\t**ESCALATED** (run-record `evals/run-records/pinewood-derby-sim/0001-physics-engine.json`;\n46\thuman summary `features/0001-physics-engine/ESCALATION.md`). Discovery symlink works. PO\n47\tdecomposed into **13 work items**; WI-1..3 passed, WI-4 & WI-5 hit loop caps (escalated), WI-6\n48\tinterrupted, WI-7..13 never started. Protective gates worked as designed: the adversarial\n49\treviewer repeatedly caught a real unresolved physics defect — the **energy ledger doesn't close\n50\t/ `pe_initial` omits the transition arc**, and the **stall/DNF model is wrong** (light stable\n51\tcars flagged as crashes; stalled cars grind the 60s guard → blows the <5ms NFR). On-disk: 220\n52\ttests pass, 1 red (AC-E4, the ledger defect's signature — left red, not papered over). args note:\n53\tbuild-loop needs prdRef/trdRef/profileRef as a real JSON object (a stringified args bails at\n54\tvalidation). Two eval-loop signals: (a) recurring **\"subagent completed without calling\n55\tStructuredOutput\"** crash (5×) on long physics-dev sessions; (b) the full suite runs each green\n56\tgate, so a later WI's edit can regress an earlier WI's accepted test (WI-6 regressed WI-5 AC-E4).\n57\t\n58\tUPDATE (2026-06-03): the escalation was resolved + the feature finished. (1) Manual focused fix\n59\tof the energy/DNF root defect: removed the WI-6 \"head-start velocity\" (car now starts at REST →\n60\tw_gravity is pure geometry, ledger closes to true KE ~1e-14); placement advantage now modelled\n61\tas rear-bias-unloads-front-wheels → less front-wheel rail-tracking friction (real derby physics,\n62\tno fabricated KE). (2) Added a backward-compatible `scopeNote` arg to build-loop.mjs for\n63\tINCREMENTAL builds (PO decomposes only remaining ACs; agents must not rebuild/weaken existing\n64\ttests) — reusable factory capability. (3) Re-ran build-loop scoped to WI-7..WI-13: COMPLETED,\n65\t**PO signed off all 30 ACs + 8 NFRs**, suite GREEN (316 tests), ruff+mypy-strict clean, cov 98%.\n66\t\n67\t**0001-physics-engine is DONE** (Eric accepted 2026-06-03). It had been escalated only because\n68\tWI-12 hit the adversarial cap with 2 open HIGH findings; Eric adjudicated both as adversarial\n69\tOVER-REACH beyond AC scope: WI12-ADV-005 tests the lever ordering on a non-baseline config\n70\t(AC-ED1/A6 pins only top/bottom for THE one baseline); WI12-ADV-006 calls a worst-case-friction\n71\tstable car a DNF (it stalls 0.29m short — consistent with the WI-5 stall=DNF ruling, and a\n72\tworst-possible build legitimately falling short is fine). WI-7's cap-finding was stale. The one\n73\tfair point in WI12-ADV-006 was a PRESENTATION concern (DNF conflates \"crashed/unstable\" with\n74\t\"ran out of speed short\"), logged as open-question q3 on **0003-web-front-end** for the kid-facing\n75\ttranslation layer to disambiguate (engine already records where/why the car stopped). Records:\n76\tevals/run-records/pinewood-derby-sim/0001-physics-engine.json (status=completed; WI-12 cap-hit\n77\tpreserved at item level) + -run1-escalated.json; human summary in the feature's ESCALATION.md.\n78\tfeature.metrics_rollup set. Final build: 316 tests green, ruff+mypy-strict clean, cov 98%.\n79\t\n80\tOBSERVATIONS for the eval-loop: (a) the \"subagent completed without calling StructuredOutput\"\n81\tcrash recurred in runs 1–2 but NOT the incremental run; (b) the build-loop does NOT gate on\n82\tQA-red `red_confirmed` (it records but proceeds), which is what let the incremental run add\n83\tcharacterization tests to already-implemented physics; (c) the adversarial reviewer twice\n84\tescalated findings that probe outside the AC's stated scope (A6) — a charter/prompt-scope signal.\n85\t\n86\tNEXT: get Eric's call on WI-12 (likely → `done`). Then run `workflows/eval-loop.mjs` (auditors +\n87\tsynthesizer) over the run-records to populate audits/changesets — the factory's self-improvement\n88\tstep, not yet exercised.\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55f4d0f9-3f78-404c-9d9b-b1c51c035e71","uuid":"7c2fe66c-2b69-430a-a517-9d93fc5e8327","timestamp":"2026-06-03T03:44:28.860Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ericburdett/.claude/projects/-Users-ericburdett-Projects/memory/agentic-sdlc-factory.md","content":"---\nname: agentic-sdlc-factory\ndescription: \"Ongoing design of a self-improving multi-agent SDLC \\\"factory\\\" at ~/Projects/agentic-sdlc\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 800a79a5-f568-48d8-aee9-a453e54892c9\n---\n\nThe user is designing a **self-improving SDLC \"factory\"** — a deterministic multi-agent workflow\nthat builds apps (planner → PRD/TRD → TDD build loop → adversarial review → PO sign-off) and then\naudits *how it built* the feature to auto-improve its own agents/prompts/skills/hooks.\n\nLives at `~/Projects/agentic-sdlc/` (NOT a git repo yet). Full design in `ARCHITECTURE.md`.\nKey decisions already made (see §11 decisions log there before re-deriving):\n- **Factory ⇄ products** separation; every learning has a **scope** (app-specific / archetype /\n  factory-general) = \"planes\" projected onto each lever (skill/hook/prompt/agent/workflow).\n- **Two-tier eval:** per-agent **auditor** (objective, observe-not-prescribe, always-on) →\n  **synthesizer** (correlates, classifies scope+blast-radius, emits auto-applied changeset).\n- **Guardrails:** commit every change (revertible); blast-radius tiering; protective agents (PO,\n  adversarial) never tuned toward leniency (\"don't silence your critics\"); synthesizer reads the\n  corpus not a single run.\n- Improvements **auto-apply** (no human review) — user's explicit choice; recoverability via\n  commits substitutes for review.\n\nArtifacts done: `charters/*.md` (7 role rubrics), `schema/run-record.schema.json`,\n`apps/_TEMPLATE/profile.md`, `gates.md` (definition-of-done + verdict schema per step — the\ncontrol-flow contract, distinct from charter rubrics), and the two workflow scripts\n`workflows/build-loop.mjs` + `workflows/eval-loop.mjs` (drafted, not yet run). First app chosen:\n**pinewood-derby-sim** (frontend; TS/React/Vitest; teaches kids derby physics; educational\naccuracy is a hard requirement) at `apps/pinewood-derby-sim/profile.md`.\n\nDecisions: v1 builds work items **sequentially** (shared codebase; parallel-worktree is later).\n**First app is Python 3.12 via uv** (pytest/ruff/mypy; NO Node anywhere; `uv run <cmd>` is the\ncommand pattern in the profile) — engine-first, pure physics engine, pygame UI deferred; archetype\n`desktop-app`.\n\nDONE: 7 agent defs in `agentic-sdlc/.claude/agents/` (wrap charters; tools scoped — auditor/\nsynthesizer read-only). `git init` + baseline commit done. Python venv + tooling installed and all\n3 gate commands verified passing on the scaffold. Agent discovery wired via symlink\n`~/Projects/.claude/agents → agentic-sdlc/.claude/agents` — **UNVERIFIED until a workflow runs**\n(cwd project root is ~/Projects, not the factory).\n\nDONE (2026-06-02): first real **build-loop** run of `0001-physics-engine` completed and\n**ESCALATED** (run-record `evals/run-records/pinewood-derby-sim/0001-physics-engine.json`;\nhuman summary `features/0001-physics-engine/ESCALATION.md`). Discovery symlink works. PO\ndecomposed into **13 work items**; WI-1..3 passed, WI-4 & WI-5 hit loop caps (escalated), WI-6\ninterrupted, WI-7..13 never started. Protective gates worked as designed: the adversarial\nreviewer repeatedly caught a real unresolved physics defect — the **energy ledger doesn't close\n/ `pe_initial` omits the transition arc**, and the **stall/DNF model is wrong** (light stable\ncars flagged as crashes; stalled cars grind the 60s guard → blows the <5ms NFR). On-disk: 220\ntests pass, 1 red (AC-E4, the ledger defect's signature — left red, not papered over). args note:\nbuild-loop needs prdRef/trdRef/profileRef as a real JSON object (a stringified args bails at\nvalidation). Two eval-loop signals: (a) recurring **\"subagent completed without calling\nStructuredOutput\"** crash (5×) on long physics-dev sessions; (b) the full suite runs each green\ngate, so a later WI's edit can regress an earlier WI's accepted test (WI-6 regressed WI-5 AC-E4).\n\nUPDATE (2026-06-03): the escalation was resolved + the feature finished. (1) Manual focused fix\nof the energy/DNF root defect: removed the WI-6 \"head-start velocity\" (car now starts at REST →\nw_gravity is pure geometry, ledger closes to true KE ~1e-14); placement advantage now modelled\nas rear-bias-unloads-front-wheels → less front-wheel rail-tracking friction (real derby physics,\nno fabricated KE). (2) Added a backward-compatible `scopeNote` arg to build-loop.mjs for\nINCREMENTAL builds (PO decomposes only remaining ACs; agents must not rebuild/weaken existing\ntests) — reusable factory capability. (3) Re-ran build-loop scoped to WI-7..WI-13: COMPLETED,\n**PO signed off all 30 ACs + 8 NFRs**, suite GREEN (316 tests), ruff+mypy-strict clean, cov 98%.\n\n**0001-physics-engine is DONE** (Eric accepted 2026-06-03). It had been escalated only because\nWI-12 hit the adversarial cap with 2 open HIGH findings; Eric adjudicated both as adversarial\nOVER-REACH beyond AC scope: WI12-ADV-005 tests the lever ordering on a non-baseline config\n(AC-ED1/A6 pins only top/bottom for THE one baseline); WI12-ADV-006 calls a worst-case-friction\nstable car a DNF (it stalls 0.29m short — consistent with the WI-5 stall=DNF ruling, and a\nworst-possible build legitimately falling short is fine). WI-7's cap-finding was stale. The one\nfair point in WI12-ADV-006 was a PRESENTATION concern (DNF conflates \"crashed/unstable\" with\n\"ran out of speed short\"), logged as open-question q3 on **0003-web-front-end** for the kid-facing\ntranslation layer to disambiguate (engine already records where/why the car stopped). Records:\nevals/run-records/pinewood-derby-sim/0001-physics-engine.json (status=completed; WI-12 cap-hit\npreserved at item level) + -run1-escalated.json; human summary in the feature's ESCALATION.md.\nfeature.metrics_rollup set. Final build: 316 tests green, ruff+mypy-strict clean, cov 98%.\n\nOBSERVATIONS for the eval-loop: (a) the \"subagent completed without calling StructuredOutput\"\ncrash recurred in runs 1–2 but NOT the incremental run; (b) the build-loop does NOT gate on\nQA-red `red_confirmed` (it records but proceeds), which is what let the incremental run add\ncharacterization tests to already-implemented physics; (c) the adversarial reviewer twice\nescalated findings that probe outside the AC's stated scope (A6) — a charter/prompt-scope signal.\n\nNEXT: get Eric's call on WI-12 (likely → `done`). Then run `workflows/eval-loop.mjs` (auditors +\nsynthesizer) over the run-records to populate audits/changesets — the factory's self-improvement\nstep, not yet exercised.\n","numLines":89,"startLine":1,"totalLines":89}}}
