{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AE4shqVTjDQXJyThQLdhLm","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Gate Criteria — Definition of Done per step\n2\t\n3\t> **Two kinds of criteria — don't confuse them:**\n4\t> - **Charter rubric** (`charters/*.md`) — quality dimensions the **auditor scores 0–5**. Feeds\n5\t>   *improvement*. Soft, graded.\n6\t> - **Gate criteria (this doc)** — the **binary/threshold pass condition the workflow script\n7\t>   branches on**. Feeds *control flow*. Hard, decided.\n8\t>\n9\t> Every gating agent returns a **structured verdict** (schemas below, mirrored in the workflow\n10\t> scripts). The script advances on pass, loops/escalates on fail — no human in the inner loop.\n11\t> Prefer **machine-checkable** conditions (run the command, read the exit code/diff) over\n12\t> opinion wherever possible; that's why \"did tests go green\" beats \"looks done\".\n13\t\n14\t---\n15\t\n16\t## Step 0 — PO Decompose (transform, has a DoD)\n17\t**Done when:** every PRD acceptance criterion maps to ≥1 work item; each item is independently\n18\ttestable and vertically sliced; dependency order is explicit.\n19\t**Verdict:** `{ work_items: [{ id, title, acceptance_criteria[], depends_on[] }] }`\n20\t**Fail action:** re-decompose (criteria unmapped or items not testable).\n21\t\n22\t## Step 1 — QA Red gate (write failing tests)\n23\t**Pass when (all true):**\n24\t- A test exists for **every** acceptance criterion of the work item.\n25\t- The suite **runs** (profile `commands.test`).\n26\t- The new tests **FAIL** — and fail **for the right reason** (true RED, not an import error).\n27\t- Tests are **deterministic** (seeded; no clock/network/random nondeterminism).\n28\t- **No implementation written yet.**\n29\t**Machine check:** run `test`; confirm new tests present and failing.\n30\t**Verdict:** `{ red_confirmed, deterministic, tests:[{criterion, test_id, failing, fails_for_right_reason}] }`\n31\t**Fail action:** QA revises tests (not a developer hand-off until RED is true).\n32\t\n33\t## Step 2 — Developer Green gate (make tests pass)\n34\t**Pass when (all true):**\n35\t- Full suite **green** (`commands.test`).\n36\t- `commands.lint` and `commands.typecheck` pass.\n37\t- **No test files modified, skipped, or deleted** (integrity — checked against the diff).\n38\t- Changes scoped to the work item (no unrelated edits).\n39\t**Machine check:** run test/lint/typecheck; `git diff --name-only` shows no test-path changes.\n40\t**Verdict:** `{ green, lint_pass, typecheck_pass, tests_unmodified, summary }`\n41\t**Fail action:** developer iterates, capped at `caps.green` attempts → escalate.\n42\t\n43\t## Step 3 — QA Validate gate (vs acceptance criteria)\n44\t**Pass when (all true):**\n45\t- Every acceptance criterion has ≥1 **passing** test mapped to it (traceability).\n46\t- Coverage meets the profile `quality_bars.coverage`.\n47\t- No `skip`/`only`/`xfail` hiding work; assertions are behavioral, not implementation-coupled.\n48\t**Verdict:** `{ validated, coverage, criteria:[{criterion, covered_by[], passing}], unmapped[] }`\n49\t**Fail action:** loop back to QA red / developer for the unmapped or failing criteria.\n50\t\n51\t## Step 4 — Adversarial Review gate (loop)\n52\t**The reviewer must work a coverage checklist** (this is \"what the adversarial reviewer is\n53\tthinking about\"):\n54\t1. **Boundaries** — min/max/zero/empty/overflow, off-by-one.\n55\t2. **Error & exception paths** — every failure mode handled per convention.\n56\t3. **Concurrency / ordering** — races, re-entrancy, state across calls.\n57\t4. **Input validation** — malformed, hostile, out-of-range, wrong-type input.\n58\t5. **Resource / performance** — exhaustion, large inputs, the profile perf budget.\n59\t6. **Domain correctness** — archetype/app-specific (for the derby sim: does extreme input\n60\t   produce physically *wrong* results or violate the real priority order?).\n61\t\n62\t**Loop-exit (pass) when:** a full checklist pass yields **zero new findings at/above the severity\n63\tthreshold** (default: no open `high`/`critical`), each finding reproducible (repro steps or a\n64\tfailing test).\n65\t**Loop:** findings → QA writes covering tests (Step 1) → developer fixes to green (Step 2) →\n66\tre-review. Capped at `caps.adversarial` iterations → **escalate to user**.\n67\t**Verdict (per pass):** `{ findings:[{id, category, severity, description, repro, reproducible}], categories_checked[] }`\n68\t\n69\t## Step 5 — PO Sign-off gate (acceptance)\n70\t**Pass when (all true):**\n71\t- **Every** PRD/TRD acceptance criterion is marked **met with evidence** (a passing test or\n72\t  demonstrated behavior).\n73\t- All NFRs from the profile `quality_bars` are satisfied with evidence.\n74\t- **Zero** unmet criteria.\n75\t**Verdict:** `{ signed_off, criteria:[{criterion, met, evidence}], unmet[], nfr:[{name, met, evidence}] }`\n76\t**Protective gate:** the bar only ever moves *stricter* — never relaxed by the synthesizer.\n77\t**Fail action:** loop back with the specific unmet criteria; on repeat failure → escalate.\n78\t\n79\t---\n80\t\n81\t## Auditor — what it bases judgment on (completeness contract, not a gate)\n82\t- **Basis:** the audited role's **charter rubric** + that agent's **transcript** + the **inputs it\n83\t  was given**. Judges *behavior*, not intent (no chain-of-thought available).\n84\t- **Done when:** every charter dimension scored 0–5 **with transcript evidence**; observations\n85\t  typed (`friction|assumption|missing_input|inefficiency|strength`) and evidence-linked;\n86\t  self-report validated against behavior; output conforms to the run-record `audit` schema.\n87\t- **Must NOT:** prescribe fixes, make cross-agent claims, or grade product code. An audit that\n88\t  prescribes is itself a defect.\n89\t\n90\t## Synthesizer (system evaluator) — what it bases judgment on\n91\t- **Basis:** all **audits** + the **objective metrics** (run-record `metrics`) + the **corpus**\n92\t  (recurrence) + the run-record **schema** (to critique the measurement).\n93\t- **Act-vs-log rule:** only emit an **actionable** change when it (a) traces to a root cause\n94\t  correlated across **≥2 signals** AND (b) is **corpus-supported as recurring** (≥ `minOccurrences`).\n95\t  One-offs are **logged, not applied.**\n96\t- **Each change must carry:** `root_cause`, `lever` (cheapest/hardest-enforcing), `scope`\n97\t  (app-specific/archetype/factory-general — never contaminate the factory with an app quirk),\n98\t  `blast_tier`, and for high/highest tiers **validation before a discrete revertible commit**.\n99\t- **Hard guards:** never edit a protective agent (PO, adversarial) toward leniency; never weaken\n100\t  the measurement; surface `measurement_gaps` when audits cite signal the metrics don't capture.\n101\t\n102\t---\n103\t\n104\t## Shared constants (used by the workflow scripts)\n105\t- **Severity order:** `critical(4) > high(3) > medium(2) > low(1)`.\n106\t- **Adversarial block threshold:** default `high` (findings ≥ high block loop exit).\n107\t- **Caps:** `caps.green` (developer attempts, default 6), `caps.adversarial` (review iterations,\n108\t  default 3). Hitting a cap → **escalate to user**, never silent pass.\n109\t- **minOccurrences:** default 2 (corpus support required before the synthesizer acts).\n110\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55f4d0f9-3f78-404c-9d9b-b1c51c035e71","uuid":"972e197d-0c8f-4295-bf51-8ab6c31ccc7e","timestamp":"2026-06-03T03:45:06.957Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ericburdett/Projects/agentic-sdlc/gates.md","content":"# Gate Criteria — Definition of Done per step\n\n> **Two kinds of criteria — don't confuse them:**\n> - **Charter rubric** (`charters/*.md`) — quality dimensions the **auditor scores 0–5**. Feeds\n>   *improvement*. Soft, graded.\n> - **Gate criteria (this doc)** — the **binary/threshold pass condition the workflow script\n>   branches on**. Feeds *control flow*. Hard, decided.\n>\n> Every gating agent returns a **structured verdict** (schemas below, mirrored in the workflow\n> scripts). The script advances on pass, loops/escalates on fail — no human in the inner loop.\n> Prefer **machine-checkable** conditions (run the command, read the exit code/diff) over\n> opinion wherever possible; that's why \"did tests go green\" beats \"looks done\".\n\n---\n\n## Step 0 — PO Decompose (transform, has a DoD)\n**Done when:** every PRD acceptance criterion maps to ≥1 work item; each item is independently\ntestable and vertically sliced; dependency order is explicit.\n**Verdict:** `{ work_items: [{ id, title, acceptance_criteria[], depends_on[] }] }`\n**Fail action:** re-decompose (criteria unmapped or items not testable).\n\n## Step 1 — QA Red gate (write failing tests)\n**Pass when (all true):**\n- A test exists for **every** acceptance criterion of the work item.\n- The suite **runs** (profile `commands.test`).\n- The new tests **FAIL** — and fail **for the right reason** (true RED, not an import error).\n- Tests are **deterministic** (seeded; no clock/network/random nondeterminism).\n- **No implementation written yet.**\n**Machine check:** run `test`; confirm new tests present and failing.\n**Verdict:** `{ red_confirmed, deterministic, tests:[{criterion, test_id, failing, fails_for_right_reason}] }`\n**Fail action:** QA revises tests (not a developer hand-off until RED is true).\n\n## Step 2 — Developer Green gate (make tests pass)\n**Pass when (all true):**\n- Full suite **green** (`commands.test`).\n- `commands.lint` and `commands.typecheck` pass.\n- **No test files modified, skipped, or deleted** (integrity — checked against the diff).\n- Changes scoped to the work item (no unrelated edits).\n**Machine check:** run test/lint/typecheck; `git diff --name-only` shows no test-path changes.\n**Verdict:** `{ green, lint_pass, typecheck_pass, tests_unmodified, summary }`\n**Fail action:** developer iterates, capped at `caps.green` attempts → escalate.\n\n## Step 3 — QA Validate gate (vs acceptance criteria)\n**Pass when (all true):**\n- Every acceptance criterion has ≥1 **passing** test mapped to it (traceability).\n- Coverage meets the profile `quality_bars.coverage`.\n- No `skip`/`only`/`xfail` hiding work; assertions are behavioral, not implementation-coupled.\n**Verdict:** `{ validated, coverage, criteria:[{criterion, covered_by[], passing}], unmapped[] }`\n**Fail action:** loop back to QA red / developer for the unmapped or failing criteria.\n\n## Step 4 — Adversarial Review gate (loop)\n**The reviewer must work a coverage checklist** (this is \"what the adversarial reviewer is\nthinking about\"):\n1. **Boundaries** — min/max/zero/empty/overflow, off-by-one.\n2. **Error & exception paths** — every failure mode handled per convention.\n3. **Concurrency / ordering** — races, re-entrancy, state across calls.\n4. **Input validation** — malformed, hostile, out-of-range, wrong-type input.\n5. **Resource / performance** — exhaustion, large inputs, the profile perf budget.\n6. **Domain correctness** — archetype/app-specific (for the derby sim: does extreme input\n   produce physically *wrong* results or violate the real priority order?).\n\n**Loop-exit (pass) when:** a full checklist pass yields **zero new findings at/above the severity\nthreshold** (default: no open `high`/`critical`), each finding reproducible (repro steps or a\nfailing test).\n**Loop:** findings → QA writes covering tests (Step 1) → developer fixes to green (Step 2) →\nre-review. Capped at `caps.adversarial` iterations → **escalate to user**.\n**Verdict (per pass):** `{ findings:[{id, category, severity, description, repro, reproducible}], categories_checked[] }`\n\n## Step 5 — PO Sign-off gate (acceptance)\n**Pass when (all true):**\n- **Every** PRD/TRD acceptance criterion is marked **met with evidence** (a passing test or\n  demonstrated behavior).\n- All NFRs from the profile `quality_bars` are satisfied with evidence.\n- **Zero** unmet criteria.\n**Verdict:** `{ signed_off, criteria:[{criterion, met, evidence}], unmet[], nfr:[{name, met, evidence}] }`\n**Protective gate:** the bar only ever moves *stricter* — never relaxed by the synthesizer.\n**Fail action:** loop back with the specific unmet criteria; on repeat failure → escalate.\n\n---\n\n## Auditor — what it bases judgment on (completeness contract, not a gate)\n- **Basis:** the audited role's **charter rubric** + that agent's **transcript** + the **inputs it\n  was given**. Judges *behavior*, not intent (no chain-of-thought available).\n- **Done when:** every charter dimension scored 0–5 **with transcript evidence**; observations\n  typed (`friction|assumption|missing_input|inefficiency|strength`) and evidence-linked;\n  self-report validated against behavior; output conforms to the run-record `audit` schema.\n- **Must NOT:** prescribe fixes, make cross-agent claims, or grade product code. An audit that\n  prescribes is itself a defect.\n\n## Synthesizer (system evaluator) — what it bases judgment on\n- **Basis:** all **audits** + the **objective metrics** (run-record `metrics`) + the **corpus**\n  (recurrence) + the run-record **schema** (to critique the measurement).\n- **Act-vs-log rule:** only emit an **actionable** change when it (a) traces to a root cause\n  correlated across **≥2 signals** AND (b) is **corpus-supported as recurring** (≥ `minOccurrences`).\n  One-offs are **logged, not applied.**\n- **Each change must carry:** `root_cause`, `lever` (cheapest/hardest-enforcing), `scope`\n  (app-specific/archetype/factory-general — never contaminate the factory with an app quirk),\n  `blast_tier`, and for high/highest tiers **validation before a discrete revertible commit**.\n- **Hard guards:** never edit a protective agent (PO, adversarial) toward leniency; never weaken\n  the measurement; surface `measurement_gaps` when audits cite signal the metrics don't capture.\n\n---\n\n## Shared constants (used by the workflow scripts)\n- **Severity order:** `critical(4) > high(3) > medium(2) > low(1)`.\n- **Adversarial block threshold:** default `high` (findings ≥ high block loop exit).\n- **Caps:** `caps.green` (developer attempts, default 6), `caps.adversarial` (review iterations,\n  default 3). Hitting a cap → **escalate to user**, never silent pass.\n- **minOccurrences:** default 2 (corpus support required before the synthesizer acts).\n","numLines":110,"startLine":1,"totalLines":110}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01AvHv9Um6VJwPVmQr1fuyPj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01T25Yk4wiu4rPAHShm9PUx9","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ericburdett/Projects/agentic-sdlc/apps/pinewood-derby-sim/features/0003-web-front-end/TRD.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10469,"cache_read_input_tokens":35314,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10469},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55f4d0f9-3f78-404c-9d9b-b1c51c035e71","uuid":"9c1a9886-4204-4e0f-a804-46759727fddc","request_id":"req_011Cbfdxr8bJm123pSzKjfgM"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T25Yk4wiu4rPAHShm9PUx9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# TRD — Web Front-End (Interactive Car Builder & Race UI)\n2\t\n3\t- **App:** pinewood-derby-sim · **Feature:** `0003-web-front-end`\n4\t- **Status:** approved — 2026-06-02\n5\t- **Companion:** [`PRD.md`](./PRD.md) · **Engine contract:** [`0001-physics-engine/TRD.md`](../0001-physics-engine/TRD.md) ·\n6\t  **Domain truth:** [`docs/physics-spec.md`](../../docs/physics-spec.md) · **Profile:** [`profile.md`](../../profile.md)\n7\t- **Last updated:** 2026-06-02\n8\t\n9\tThis TRD describes *how* to build the front-end specified in the PRD. It honors the profile's hard\n10\tconstraints (no network at runtime, no PII, safe for children, engine stays pure & dependency-free)\n11\tand the platform decision (static web + Pyodide on GitHub Pages). It also flags where this feature\n12\t**expands the app's stack** beyond pure Python.\n13\t\n14\t---\n15\t\n16\t## 1. Architecture overview\n17\t\n18\tA **static single-page app** with the **pure Python engine running in the browser** via Pyodide.\n19\tTwo clean layers, one boundary:\n20\t\n21\t```\n22\t┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n23\t│ Browser (static site, same-origin assets, no network at runtime)  │\n24\t│                                                                    │\n25\t│  ┌── UI (TypeScript) ─────────────┐   ┌── Pyodide (WASM) ───────┐  │\n26\t│  │ Builder controls               │   │ pinewood_derby (0001)   │  │\n27\t│  │ Track <canvas> animation       │   │   simulate(car) → Result│  │\n28\t│  │ Result / \"why\" panel           │◄─►│ pinewood_derby.present  │  │\n29\t│  │ Garage (localStorage)          │   │   (NEW pure translation)│  │\n30\t│  └────────────────────────────────┘   └─────────────────────────┘  │\n31\t│            ▲ JS ↔ Python bridge (Pyodide proxies, JSON-able DTOs)   │\n32\t└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n33\t        hosted on GitHub Pages (static files only)\n34\t```\n35\t\n36\t- **Engine stays pure & untouched** (`0001`). The front-end imports it; it adds **no physics**\n37\t  (PRD AC-G1).\n38\t- **Translation layer = the folded `0002`**, implemented as a **new pure Python module**\n39\t  `pinewood_derby/present.py` (DOM-free, unit-tested with `pytest`). It maps `RaceResult` +\n40\t  `CarDesign` → a **JSON-serializable view-model** the JS UI renders. Keeping it in Python (a) reuses\n41\t  the profile's `uv run pytest` bar, (b) keeps all \"what does this number mean\" logic on one side of\n42\t  the bridge, and (c) ports for free if the app is ever re-hosted.\n43\t- **UI is thin TypeScript:** read controls → build a `CarDesign` (in Python, over the bridge) →\n44\t  `simulate` → `present` → render the returned view-model + animate the trajectory. No physics, no\n45\t  domain rules duplicated in JS.\n46\t\n47\t## 2. Platform & hosting\n48\t\n49\t- **Pyodide, vendored same-origin.** The Pyodide runtime (`.js` + `.wasm` + stdlib) and the\n50\t  `pinewood_derby` package (shipped as a **pure-Python wheel** built from `0001`, or loaded as source\n51\t  via `loadPackage`/`pyodide.FS`) are committed/copied into the published site. **No CDN** — required\n52\t  by PRD AC-P1 (no third-party calls) and to work offline (AC-P3).\n53\t- **GitHub Pages.** Static hosting; a CI workflow builds the site (Vite) + the engine wheel and\n54\t  publishes to Pages. Pages cannot run server code — fine, there is none. *(Single-threaded Pyodide\n55\t  only; we do **not** use `SharedArrayBuffer`/threads, so the COOP/COEP headers Pages can't set are\n56\t  not needed.)*\n57\t- **Offline (AC-P3).** A **service worker** precaches all static assets (HTML/JS/CSS/Pyodide/wheel)\n58\t  so the app loads offline after the first visit. The SW makes no network fetches of its own.\n59\t\n60\t## 3. Component / module layout\n61\t\n62\t```\n63\tweb/                              # NEW front-end workspace (TypeScript + Vite)\n64\t  index.html\n65\t  src/\n66\t    main.ts                       # bootstrap: load Pyodide, wire UI\n67\t    pyodide-bridge.ts             # load runtime + engine wheel; typed call wrappers\n68\t    controls/                     # builder inputs → control-state\n69\t      controls.ts                 # six levers + weight; constrained to valid domains (AC-C1)\n70\t      presets.ts                  # default car (AC-C2) + named \"good/bad build\" demo presets\n71\t    race/\n72\t      animator.ts                 # <canvas> 2-D side-view; plays RaceResult.trajectory (AC-R1/R2)\n73\t    result/\n74\t      result-view.ts              # renders the view-model: time, \"where did your speed go\", \"why\"\n75\t    garage/\n76\t      garage.ts                   # save/list/load/delete via localStorage (AC-S1/2/3)\n77\t    a11y/, styles/                # focus management, WCAG-AA theme (AC-A1/A2/A3)\n78\t  sw.ts                           # service worker: precache static assets (AC-P3)\n79\t  public/pyodide/                 # vendored Pyodide runtime (same-origin, no CDN)\n80\t  tests-e2e/                      # Playwright headless-browser specs (UI ACs)\n81\t\n82\tsrc/pinewood_derby/\n83\t  present.py                      # NEW pure translation layer (the folded 0002)\n84\ttests/\n85\t  test_present.py                # NEW pytest unit tests for present.py\n86\t```\n87\t\n88\tThe Python side adds exactly **one** new module (`present.py`) to the existing pure package; all UI\n89\tlives under the new `web/` workspace.\n90\t\n91\t## 4. Translation layer — `pinewood_derby/present.py` (pure, the folded 0002)\n92\t\n93\tA pure function from engine output to a kid-facing, JSON-serializable view-model. **No DOM, no I/O,\n94\tno physics, no technical units** (PRD AC-X3).\n95\t\n96\t```python\n97\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\n98\tclass LossBar:\n99\t    key: str            # \"air\" | \"axle\" | \"rails\" | \"wheels\" | \"kept\"\n100\t    label: str          # plain language, e.g. \"Axle friction\"\n101\t    proportion: float   # 0..1 share of the energy story (for bar length); NOT joules\n102\t    is_kept: bool       # the \"speed you kept\" bar vs a loss\n103\t\n104\tOutcome = Literal[\"finished\", \"tipped\", \"stalled\"]   # AC-R4: two distinct non-finish stories\n105\t\n106\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\n107\tclass RaceView:\n108\t    finished: bool\n109\t    outcome: Outcome                  # \"finished\" | \"tipped\" (wobble/crash) | \"stalled\" (ran out of speed) — AC-R4\n110\t    time_seconds: float | None        # None for any non-finish (PRD AC-R2); seconds is allowed (A7)\n111\t    stopped_distance_frac: float | None  # for \"stalled\": how far it got (0..1), to say \"stopped just short\"\n112\t    legal_weight: bool\n113\t    headline: str                     # \"Nice! 2.91 seconds.\" / \"Your car wobbled and tipped.\" / \"Ran out of speed, just short.\"\n114\t    breakdown: tuple[LossBar, ...]    # ranked largest-first (AC-X1)\n115\t    why: str                          # dominant-factor coaching tied to a real principle (AC-X2); outcome-specific for non-finishes\n116\t    tips: tuple[str, ...]             # 1–3 next-step suggestions, priority-ordered (AC-X4)\n117\t    trajectory: tuple[FramePoint, ...]# down-sampled points the animator replays\n118\t\n119\tdef present(result: RaceResult, car: CarDesign) -> RaceView: ...\n120\tdef to_json(view: RaceView) -> dict: ...   # plain dict for the JS bridge\n121\t```\n122\t\n123\t- **\"Where did your speed go?\" (AC-X1, A8):** map ledger fields → bars —\n124\t  `w_drag`→`air`, `w_axle`→`axle`, `w_rail`→`rails`, `ke_rotational_final`→`wheels`,\n125\t  final linear KE→`kept`. Normalize to proportions of the **energy actually delivered on this run** —\n126\t  i.e. the **integrated gravity work `w_gravity`** (which the per-force ledger closes against:\n127\t  `w_gravity − w_drag − w_axle − w_rail = ke_linear + ke_rotational`), **not `pe_initial`** — so the\n128\t  bars sum to ~1 for *both* a finisher and a stalled car (a stalled car descends only part of the\n129\t  ramp, so `w_gravity < pe_initial`). **Guard the all-zero ledger** (a `tipped` DNF has\n130\t  `w_gravity == 0`): emit **no breakdown bars** for a tip — its story is the wobble headline, not a\n131\t  loss chart. **Rank largest-first.**\n132\t- **\"Why\" (AC-X2, AC-X4):** pick the **largest *loss*** bar and emit the matching plain-language\n133\t  principle from a small, reviewed lookup table (axle→polish & graphite; rails→fix alignment /\n134\t  rail-ride; air→smoother/lower body; wheels→lighter, truer wheels; plus weight/placement coaching\n135\t  driven by `legal_weight` and `car.com_ahead_of_rear_axle`). The table encodes the **real priority\n136\t  order**, so tips never invert it (aero is never advised over weight/friction). A **banned-terms\n137\t  guard** (shared with the test) keeps jargon out.\n138\t- **Non-finish disambiguation (AC-R2 / AC-R4):** `finished=False`, `time_seconds=None`, then classify\n139\t  the single engine `outcome=DNF` into **two** view outcomes **from the trajectory + ledger** (verified\n140\t  against `engine.py`/`result.py` 2026-06-02):\n141\t  - **`tipped`** — the engine short-circuits an unstable car (front-load fraction `d_COM/L` below the\n142\t    cliff) **before the run starts**: the result has a **single `trajectory` point at `position == 0`**\n143\t    and an **all-zero work ledger** (`w_gravity == w_drag == w_axle == w_rail == 0`,\n144\t    `ke_*_final == 0`). Detect via `len(trajectory) == 1 and trajectory[0].position == 0.0`. Headline +\n145\t    \"why\" speak to **wobble/tip**: weight too far back / past the stability cliff. `stopped_distance_frac\n146\t    = 0.0`.\n147\t  - **`stalled`** — the car ran but its velocity hit zero **before** the finish: a **multi-point\n148\t    trajectory** whose **last `position` satisfies `0 < position < track_length`**, with\n149\t    `finish_velocity ≈ 0` and a non-trivial ledger. Record `stopped_distance_frac = last_position /\n150\t    track_length` and speak to **\"ran out of speed and stopped just short\"**: too much friction / not\n151\t    enough starting energy — *not* a crash. *(The rare 60 s wall-clock guard — a near-stationary crawl —\n152\t    also lands here and is messaged as a stall.)*\n153\t  - **Discriminator note:** `normal_forces` is a **single static `(front, rear)` pair** computed once on\n154\t    the flat (`result.py`), **not** a per-frame series, and `front = M·g·(d_COM/L) ≥ 0` always — so it\n155\t    is **not** usable to detect a tip. The trajectory/ledger signals above are the real evidence.\n156\t  The classifier reads only `outcome`, `trajectory`, and the ledger — no new physics (AC-G1).\n157\t- **Purity:** frozen dataclasses, deterministic, ≥ 90% unit coverage (PRD NFR). Tested entirely\n158\t  without a browser.\n159\t\n160\t## 5. UI ↔ Python bridge\n161\t\n162\t- **Import paths (verified 2026-06-02):** `pinewood_derby/__init__.py` does **not** re-export the\n163\t  public API (it sets `__version__` only), so the Python side imports from the **submodules** —\n164\t  `from pinewood_derby.engine import simulate`, `from pinewood_derby.car import CarDesign`,\n165\t  `from pinewood_derby.result import RaceResult`, `from pinewood_derby.track import STANDARD_TRACK`.\n166\t  Alternatively `0001` adds a one-line re-export to `__init__.py` (tracked as a tiny follow-up, PRD A4a).\n167\t- On boot, `pyodide-bridge.ts` loads the vendored runtime, then the `pinewood_derby` wheel, and\n168\t  exposes typed wrappers:\n169\t  - `buildCar(controlState) → PyProxy(CarDesign)` — constructs the design **in Python** so the\n170\t    engine's own validation is the single source of truth (PRD AC-C1); a `ValueError` is caught and\n171\t    surfaced as an inline control message, never a stack trace.\n172\t  - `race(car) → RaceView(JSON)` — calls `simulate(car, seed=FIXED_SEED)` then `present(...)`,\n173\t    returning a plain JSON object (no lingering proxies) for the renderer (AC-R3 determinism via the\n174\t    fixed seed, A6).\n175\t- Control domains in `controls.ts` mirror the engine's validation bounds so the UI **pre-constrains**\n176\t  inputs; the Python validation remains the backstop. (Two-layer guard for AC-C1.)\n177\t- `CarDesign` (de)serialization for the garage goes through a small Python `to_dict`/`from_dict`\n178\t  (or a `present.py` helper), so localStorage holds a **plain, versioned JSON** snapshot — not a\n179\t  proxy — and load reconstructs + re-validates it (AC-S2).\n180\t\n181\t## 6. Animation (`race/animator.ts`)\n182\t\n183\t- A 2-D side view of `STANDARD_TRACK` (ramp → transition arc → flat) drawn on `<canvas>`; the car\n184\t  sprite is placed each frame from `RaceResult.trajectory` (position along the arc → screen x/y, plus\n185\t  the track angle for rotation). A running clock counts up to `race_time_s`.\n186\t- **Non-finish (AC-R2/AC-R4):** a **`stalled`** car has a real multi-point trajectory, so it animates\n187\t  its run and **coasts to a visible halt short of the line** (no crash visuals). A **`tipped`** car has\n188\t  only the single at-rest start point (the engine rules it unstable before the run), so there is **no\n189\t  run to animate** — it shows a **wobble-at-the-start-line** state instead. The two are rendered\n190\t  distinctly to match their headlines.\n191\t- **Determinism:** same trajectory in ⇒ same animation out (AC-R3).\n192\t- **Perf:** `requestAnimationFrame`, target **≥ 30 fps**; the trajectory is already down-sampled\n193\t  (≤ ~500 pts by the engine), so per-frame work is trivial.\n194\t- **Duration basis:** scale playback off the **trajectory's own last `t`**, *not* `race_time_s`\n195\t  (which is `None` for a non-finisher). A finisher plays near real-time (~3–4 s). A **`stalled`** run\n196\t  can carry a much longer trajectory `t` (the engine's stall path runs up to a 60 s wall-clock guard),\n197\t  so **cap/compress** the non-finisher playback to a few legible seconds rather than replaying a\n198\t  60 s crawl. A **`tipped`** run has a single `t=0` frame, so there is no timeline to scale.\n199\t\n200\t## 7. Garage / persistence (`garage/garage.ts`)\n201\t\n202\t- `localStorage` keyed under a single namespace (e.g. `pds.garage.v1`), holding a JSON map of\n203\t  `name → { schemaVersion, design }`.\n204\t- Operations: **save** (name + current design), **list**, **load** (restore controls + re-validate),\n205\t  **delete**, **clear**. All synchronous, on-device (AC-S1/S2/S3).\n206\t- **No PII, no network** (AC-P2): the only stored data is car designs the user explicitly saves; a\n207\t  visible \"clear my garage\" control exists.\n208\t- A `schemaVersion` on each entry allows safe migration if `CarDesign` changes (relevant given the\n209\t  build is deferred until the engine contract settles — A4).\n210\t\n211\t## 8. Privacy, offline & safety (PRD AC-P1/P2/P3)\n212\t\n213\t| Requirement | Implementation |\n214\t| --- | --- |\n215\t| No network at runtime | All assets same-origin & vendored; **no CDN, no fonts/analytics/embeds**; no `fetch`/`XHR`/`WebSocket` to any origin |\n216\t| No PII / data collection | Only `localStorage` car designs; no accounts, no input fields for personal data, no telemetry |\n217\t| Works offline | Service worker precaches the full static bundle; subsequent loads need no network |\n218\t| Safe for children | Encouraging copy, no external links opened without intent; the `0004` leaderboard (the only network feature) is explicitly **not** here |\n219\t\n220\tCI/lint check: a test asserts the built bundle references **no off-origin URLs** (guards AC-P1\n221\tagainst regressions).\n222\t\n223\t## 9. Accessibility (PRD AC-A1/A2/A3)\n224\t\n225\t- Native, labeled form controls (`<input type=range>`, toggles, buttons) with `<label>`/`aria-*`;\n226\t  logical tab order; visible focus rings; **Race** reachable and operable by keyboard.\n227\t- Results announced via an `aria-live` region so a screen reader reads the time + \"why\" after a race.\n228\t- **WCAG-AA** contrast theme; **never color-only** — legal/over-limit, finish/DNF, and each loss bar\n229\t  carry text + icon. Animation respects `prefers-reduced-motion` (offer a static end-state).\n230\t- Responsive down to ~1024px; large targets for projector/Chromebook use.\n231\t\n232\t## 10. Dependencies & stack changes\n233\t\n234\t- **Python (runtime):** unchanged — `pinewood_derby` stays **stdlib-only**; `present.py` adds no\n235\t  dependency. `pyproject` `dependencies = []` holds.\n236\t- **New front-end toolchain (the stack expansion this feature introduces):**\n237\t  - **TypeScript + Vite** build; **Pyodide** vendored as a static asset.\n238\t  - **Playwright** (dev) for headless-browser UI tests; **Vitest** (or equivalent) for any pure TS\n239\t    units.\n240\t  - A **CI workflow** to build the engine wheel + the Vite bundle and deploy to GitHub Pages.\n241\t- **Profile impact (flagged, not done here):** the profile's `framework`, `commands`\n242\t  (build/test/run for the web app), `archetype` (desktop-app → web-app), deployment target, and\n243\t  audience age (→ 12–17) all need a follow-up update for consistency. Tracked as a flag for the\n244\t  synthesizer / a profile-update task (PRD §8).\n245\t\n246\t## 11. Risks & mitigations\n247\t\n248\t| Risk | Mitigation |\n249\t| --- | --- |\n250\t| **Engine contract still in flux** (`0001` building) — UI built against a moving target | **Defer build** until the contract stabilizes (A4); isolate all engine touchpoints behind `pyodide-bridge.ts` + the Python `present.py`/`to_dict`; version the garage JSON for migration |\n251\t| **Pyodide first-load weight** (several MB) hurts the Chromebook/demo experience | Show a loading state (NFR); precache via service worker so it's a one-time cost; vendor + compress assets; lazy-load nothing the first race needs |\n252\t| **Physics/units leaking to the kid** (jargon, Joules) | All translation in one pure module with a **banned-terms guard** shared by `test_present.py` and a UI text scan (AC-X3) |\n253\t| **Priority order inverted in tips** (teaching wrong order) | The \"why\"/tips lookup is **reviewed, table-driven, priority-ordered**; a domain test asserts weight/placement & friction outrank aero across sample designs (AC-X4, rides engine AC-ED1) |\n254\t| **Determinism breaks** (random seed, animation jitter) | UI pins `seed=FIXED_SEED` (A6); animation is a pure function of the returned trajectory; AC-R3 test races twice and asserts identical time/frames |\n255\t| **Accidental third-party call** (font, CDN, analytics) creeps in | Same-origin-only policy + a build test asserting **no off-origin URLs** in the bundle (AC-P1) |\n256\t| **Test stack expansion** beyond the profile's Python-only toolchain | Keep the **richest logic in pure Python** (`present.py`, `pytest`); limit browser tests to genuinely UI behavior; document the new commands for the profile update |\n257\t| **Bigger UI surface than a TDD-friendly unit** | Push testable logic into `present.py` + control-domain mapping (unit-testable); reserve Playwright for a small set of end-to-end ACs (race, DNF, save/load, no-network, keyboard) |\n258\t\n259\t## 12. Test strategy\n260\t\n261\t- **Pure translation layer (`present.py`) — `uv run pytest`, the primary bar:**\n262\t  - View-model mapping: ledger → ranked `LossBar`s largest-first (AC-X1); dominant-factor \"why\"\n263\t    selection (AC-X2); legal/over-limit headline (AC-C3).\n264\t  - **Non-finish classifier (AC-R4):** drive `present()` with **real `simulate()` output** (not\n265\t    hand-built fixtures): an unstable design (`d_COM/L` below the cliff) → `outcome=\"tipped\"`,\n266\t    `stopped_distance_frac == 0`, single-point trajectory, all-zero ledger; a stable-but-underpowered\n267\t    design (e.g. a light ~1–2 oz car that stalls short) → `outcome=\"stalled\"`,\n268\t    `0 < stopped_distance_frac < 1`, *non-crash* message. Assert the two never collapse into one and a\n269\t    slow finisher (`outcome=\"finished\"`) is neither.\n270\t  - **Banned-terms guard:** assert no jargon in any emitted string across a matrix of designs\n271\t    (AC-X3).\n272\t  - **Priority-order domain test:** across sample designs, weight/placement & friction produce the\n273\t    largest surfaced losses/tips, aero the smallest (AC-X4).\n274\t  - Determinism: `present(simulate(car, seed=S), car)` is stable (AC-R3, data side).\n275\t  - **≥ 90% coverage** on `present.py` (PRD NFR).\n276\t- **UI — Playwright (headless), one spec per UI AC:** default car loads & races (AC-C2/R1);\n277\t  out-of-range/invalid input never throws (AC-C1); over-limit raceable + flagged (AC-C3); both\n278\t  non-finish states render distinctly — `tipped` vs `stalled` (AC-R2/AC-R4); race-twice determinism\n279\t  (AC-R3); save→reload→load→race (AC-S1/S2/S3); **no off-origin\n280\t  network requests** via request interception (AC-P1); offline load after first visit (AC-P3);\n281\t  keyboard-only loop + `aria-live` result (AC-A1); not-color-only / contrast (AC-A2).\n282\t- **Engine untouched:** the `0001` suite continues to pass; a guard asserts no physics math lives\n283\t  outside `pinewood_derby` (AC-G1).\n284\t\n285\t## 13. Traceability (AC → component)\n286\t\n287\t| Area | ACs | Primary component(s) |\n288\t| --- | --- | --- |\n289\t| Controls → CarDesign | AC-C1, AC-C2, AC-C3 | `controls.ts`, `presets.ts`, `pyodide-bridge.ts` |\n290\t| Race & animation | AC-R1, AC-R2, AC-R3, AC-R4 | `animator.ts`, `pyodide-bridge.ts`, `present.py` (non-finish classifier) |\n291\t| Explanation / \"why\" | AC-X1, AC-X2, AC-X3, AC-X4 | `present.py`, `result-view.ts` |\n292\t| Garage | AC-S1, AC-S2, AC-S3 | `garage.ts`, `present.py` (to_dict/from_dict) |\n293\t| Privacy / offline / safety | AC-P1, AC-P2, AC-P3 | bundle policy, `sw.ts`, `garage.ts` |\n294\t| Accessibility | AC-A1, AC-A2, AC-A3 | `a11y/`, `styles/`, `result-view.ts` |\n295\t| Engine purity | AC-G1 | `present.py`, `pyodide-bridge.ts` |\n296\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55f4d0f9-3f78-404c-9d9b-b1c51c035e71","uuid":"545ee799-b2aa-49c3-9a62-1efa45cc4eae","timestamp":"2026-06-03T03:45:07.570Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ericburdett/Projects/agentic-sdlc/apps/pinewood-derby-sim/features/0003-web-front-end/TRD.md","content":"# TRD — Web Front-End (Interactive Car Builder & Race UI)\n\n- **App:** pinewood-derby-sim · **Feature:** `0003-web-front-end`\n- **Status:** approved — 2026-06-02\n- **Companion:** [`PRD.md`](./PRD.md) · **Engine contract:** [`0001-physics-engine/TRD.md`](../0001-physics-engine/TRD.md) ·\n  **Domain truth:** [`docs/physics-spec.md`](../../docs/physics-spec.md) · **Profile:** [`profile.md`](../../profile.md)\n- **Last updated:** 2026-06-02\n\nThis TRD describes *how* to build the front-end specified in the PRD. It honors the profile's hard\nconstraints (no network at runtime, no PII, safe for children, engine stays pure & dependency-free)\nand the platform decision (static web + Pyodide on GitHub Pages). It also flags where this feature\n**expands the app's stack** beyond pure Python.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Architecture overview\n\nA **static single-page app** with the **pure Python engine running in the browser** via Pyodide.\nTwo clean layers, one boundary:\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ Browser (static site, same-origin assets, no network at runtime)  │\n│                                                                    │\n│  ┌── UI (TypeScript) ─────────────┐   ┌── Pyodide (WASM) ───────┐  │\n│  │ Builder controls               │   │ pinewood_derby (0001)   │  │\n│  │ Track <canvas> animation       │   │   simulate(car) → Result│  │\n│  │ Result / \"why\" panel           │◄─►│ pinewood_derby.present  │  │\n│  │ Garage (localStorage)          │   │   (NEW pure translation)│  │\n│  └────────────────────────────────┘   └─────────────────────────┘  │\n│            ▲ JS ↔ Python bridge (Pyodide proxies, JSON-able DTOs)   │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n        hosted on GitHub Pages (static files only)\n```\n\n- **Engine stays pure & untouched** (`0001`). The front-end imports it; it adds **no physics**\n  (PRD AC-G1).\n- **Translation layer = the folded `0002`**, implemented as a **new pure Python module**\n  `pinewood_derby/present.py` (DOM-free, unit-tested with `pytest`). It maps `RaceResult` +\n  `CarDesign` → a **JSON-serializable view-model** the JS UI renders. Keeping it in Python (a) reuses\n  the profile's `uv run pytest` bar, (b) keeps all \"what does this number mean\" logic on one side of\n  the bridge, and (c) ports for free if the app is ever re-hosted.\n- **UI is thin TypeScript:** read controls → build a `CarDesign` (in Python, over the bridge) →\n  `simulate` → `present` → render the returned view-model + animate the trajectory. No physics, no\n  domain rules duplicated in JS.\n\n## 2. Platform & hosting\n\n- **Pyodide, vendored same-origin.** The Pyodide runtime (`.js` + `.wasm` + stdlib) and the\n  `pinewood_derby` package (shipped as a **pure-Python wheel** built from `0001`, or loaded as source\n  via `loadPackage`/`pyodide.FS`) are committed/copied into the published site. **No CDN** — required\n  by PRD AC-P1 (no third-party calls) and to work offline (AC-P3).\n- **GitHub Pages.** Static hosting; a CI workflow builds the site (Vite) + the engine wheel and\n  publishes to Pages. Pages cannot run server code — fine, there is none. *(Single-threaded Pyodide\n  only; we do **not** use `SharedArrayBuffer`/threads, so the COOP/COEP headers Pages can't set are\n  not needed.)*\n- **Offline (AC-P3).** A **service worker** precaches all static assets (HTML/JS/CSS/Pyodide/wheel)\n  so the app loads offline after the first visit. The SW makes no network fetches of its own.\n\n## 3. Component / module layout\n\n```\nweb/                              # NEW front-end workspace (TypeScript + Vite)\n  index.html\n  src/\n    main.ts                       # bootstrap: load Pyodide, wire UI\n    pyodide-bridge.ts             # load runtime + engine wheel; typed call wrappers\n    controls/                     # builder inputs → control-state\n      controls.ts                 # six levers + weight; constrained to valid domains (AC-C1)\n      presets.ts                  # default car (AC-C2) + named \"good/bad build\" demo presets\n    race/\n      animator.ts                 # <canvas> 2-D side-view; plays RaceResult.trajectory (AC-R1/R2)\n    result/\n      result-view.ts              # renders the view-model: time, \"where did your speed go\", \"why\"\n    garage/\n      garage.ts                   # save/list/load/delete via localStorage (AC-S1/2/3)\n    a11y/, styles/                # focus management, WCAG-AA theme (AC-A1/A2/A3)\n  sw.ts                           # service worker: precache static assets (AC-P3)\n  public/pyodide/                 # vendored Pyodide runtime (same-origin, no CDN)\n  tests-e2e/                      # Playwright headless-browser specs (UI ACs)\n\nsrc/pinewood_derby/\n  present.py                      # NEW pure translation layer (the folded 0002)\ntests/\n  test_present.py                # NEW pytest unit tests for present.py\n```\n\nThe Python side adds exactly **one** new module (`present.py`) to the existing pure package; all UI\nlives under the new `web/` workspace.\n\n## 4. Translation layer — `pinewood_derby/present.py` (pure, the folded 0002)\n\nA pure function from engine output to a kid-facing, JSON-serializable view-model. **No DOM, no I/O,\nno physics, no technical units** (PRD AC-X3).\n\n```python\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass LossBar:\n    key: str            # \"air\" | \"axle\" | \"rails\" | \"wheels\" | \"kept\"\n    label: str          # plain language, e.g. \"Axle friction\"\n    proportion: float   # 0..1 share of the energy story (for bar length); NOT joules\n    is_kept: bool       # the \"speed you kept\" bar vs a loss\n\nOutcome = Literal[\"finished\", \"tipped\", \"stalled\"]   # AC-R4: two distinct non-finish stories\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass RaceView:\n    finished: bool\n    outcome: Outcome                  # \"finished\" | \"tipped\" (wobble/crash) | \"stalled\" (ran out of speed) — AC-R4\n    time_seconds: float | None        # None for any non-finish (PRD AC-R2); seconds is allowed (A7)\n    stopped_distance_frac: float | None  # for \"stalled\": how far it got (0..1), to say \"stopped just short\"\n    legal_weight: bool\n    headline: str                     # \"Nice! 2.91 seconds.\" / \"Your car wobbled and tipped.\" / \"Ran out of speed, just short.\"\n    breakdown: tuple[LossBar, ...]    # ranked largest-first (AC-X1)\n    why: str                          # dominant-factor coaching tied to a real principle (AC-X2); outcome-specific for non-finishes\n    tips: tuple[str, ...]             # 1–3 next-step suggestions, priority-ordered (AC-X4)\n    trajectory: tuple[FramePoint, ...]# down-sampled points the animator replays\n\ndef present(result: RaceResult, car: CarDesign) -> RaceView: ...\ndef to_json(view: RaceView) -> dict: ...   # plain dict for the JS bridge\n```\n\n- **\"Where did your speed go?\" (AC-X1, A8):** map ledger fields → bars —\n  `w_drag`→`air`, `w_axle`→`axle`, `w_rail`→`rails`, `ke_rotational_final`→`wheels`,\n  final linear KE→`kept`. Normalize to proportions of the **energy actually delivered on this run** —\n  i.e. the **integrated gravity work `w_gravity`** (which the per-force ledger closes against:\n  `w_gravity − w_drag − w_axle − w_rail = ke_linear + ke_rotational`), **not `pe_initial`** — so the\n  bars sum to ~1 for *both* a finisher and a stalled car (a stalled car descends only part of the\n  ramp, so `w_gravity < pe_initial`). **Guard the all-zero ledger** (a `tipped` DNF has\n  `w_gravity == 0`): emit **no breakdown bars** for a tip — its story is the wobble headline, not a\n  loss chart. **Rank largest-first.**\n- **\"Why\" (AC-X2, AC-X4):** pick the **largest *loss*** bar and emit the matching plain-language\n  principle from a small, reviewed lookup table (axle→polish & graphite; rails→fix alignment /\n  rail-ride; air→smoother/lower body; wheels→lighter, truer wheels; plus weight/placement coaching\n  driven by `legal_weight` and `car.com_ahead_of_rear_axle`). The table encodes the **real priority\n  order**, so tips never invert it (aero is never advised over weight/friction). A **banned-terms\n  guard** (shared with the test) keeps jargon out.\n- **Non-finish disambiguation (AC-R2 / AC-R4):** `finished=False`, `time_seconds=None`, then classify\n  the single engine `outcome=DNF` into **two** view outcomes **from the trajectory + ledger** (verified\n  against `engine.py`/`result.py` 2026-06-02):\n  - **`tipped`** — the engine short-circuits an unstable car (front-load fraction `d_COM/L` below the\n    cliff) **before the run starts**: the result has a **single `trajectory` point at `position == 0`**\n    and an **all-zero work ledger** (`w_gravity == w_drag == w_axle == w_rail == 0`,\n    `ke_*_final == 0`). Detect via `len(trajectory) == 1 and trajectory[0].position == 0.0`. Headline +\n    \"why\" speak to **wobble/tip**: weight too far back / past the stability cliff. `stopped_distance_frac\n    = 0.0`.\n  - **`stalled`** — the car ran but its velocity hit zero **before** the finish: a **multi-point\n    trajectory** whose **last `position` satisfies `0 < position < track_length`**, with\n    `finish_velocity ≈ 0` and a non-trivial ledger. Record `stopped_distance_frac = last_position /\n    track_length` and speak to **\"ran out of speed and stopped just short\"**: too much friction / not\n    enough starting energy — *not* a crash. *(The rare 60 s wall-clock guard — a near-stationary crawl —\n    also lands here and is messaged as a stall.)*\n  - **Discriminator note:** `normal_forces` is a **single static `(front, rear)` pair** computed once on\n    the flat (`result.py`), **not** a per-frame series, and `front = M·g·(d_COM/L) ≥ 0` always — so it\n    is **not** usable to detect a tip. The trajectory/ledger signals above are the real evidence.\n  The classifier reads only `outcome`, `trajectory`, and the ledger — no new physics (AC-G1).\n- **Purity:** frozen dataclasses, deterministic, ≥ 90% unit coverage (PRD NFR). Tested entirely\n  without a browser.\n\n## 5. UI ↔ Python bridge\n\n- **Import paths (verified 2026-06-02):** `pinewood_derby/__init__.py` does **not** re-export the\n  public API (it sets `__version__` only), so the Python side imports from the **submodules** —\n  `from pinewood_derby.engine import simulate`, `from pinewood_derby.car import CarDesign`,\n  `from pinewood_derby.result import RaceResult`, `from pinewood_derby.track import STANDARD_TRACK`.\n  Alternatively `0001` adds a one-line re-export to `__init__.py` (tracked as a tiny follow-up, PRD A4a).\n- On boot, `pyodide-bridge.ts` loads the vendored runtime, then the `pinewood_derby` wheel, and\n  exposes typed wrappers:\n  - `buildCar(controlState) → PyProxy(CarDesign)` — constructs the design **in Python** so the\n    engine's own validation is the single source of truth (PRD AC-C1); a `ValueError` is caught and\n    surfaced as an inline control message, never a stack trace.\n  - `race(car) → RaceView(JSON)` — calls `simulate(car, seed=FIXED_SEED)` then `present(...)`,\n    returning a plain JSON object (no lingering proxies) for the renderer (AC-R3 determinism via the\n    fixed seed, A6).\n- Control domains in `controls.ts` mirror the engine's validation bounds so the UI **pre-constrains**\n  inputs; the Python validation remains the backstop. (Two-layer guard for AC-C1.)\n- `CarDesign` (de)serialization for the garage goes through a small Python `to_dict`/`from_dict`\n  (or a `present.py` helper), so localStorage holds a **plain, versioned JSON** snapshot — not a\n  proxy — and load reconstructs + re-validates it (AC-S2).\n\n## 6. Animation (`race/animator.ts`)\n\n- A 2-D side view of `STANDARD_TRACK` (ramp → transition arc → flat) drawn on `<canvas>`; the car\n  sprite is placed each frame from `RaceResult.trajectory` (position along the arc → screen x/y, plus\n  the track angle for rotation). A running clock counts up to `race_time_s`.\n- **Non-finish (AC-R2/AC-R4):** a **`stalled`** car has a real multi-point trajectory, so it animates\n  its run and **coasts to a visible halt short of the line** (no crash visuals). A **`tipped`** car has\n  only the single at-rest start point (the engine rules it unstable before the run), so there is **no\n  run to animate** — it shows a **wobble-at-the-start-line** state instead. The two are rendered\n  distinctly to match their headlines.\n- **Determinism:** same trajectory in ⇒ same animation out (AC-R3).\n- **Perf:** `requestAnimationFrame`, target **≥ 30 fps**; the trajectory is already down-sampled\n  (≤ ~500 pts by the engine), so per-frame work is trivial.\n- **Duration basis:** scale playback off the **trajectory's own last `t`**, *not* `race_time_s`\n  (which is `None` for a non-finisher). A finisher plays near real-time (~3–4 s). A **`stalled`** run\n  can carry a much longer trajectory `t` (the engine's stall path runs up to a 60 s wall-clock guard),\n  so **cap/compress** the non-finisher playback to a few legible seconds rather than replaying a\n  60 s crawl. A **`tipped`** run has a single `t=0` frame, so there is no timeline to scale.\n\n## 7. Garage / persistence (`garage/garage.ts`)\n\n- `localStorage` keyed under a single namespace (e.g. `pds.garage.v1`), holding a JSON map of\n  `name → { schemaVersion, design }`.\n- Operations: **save** (name + current design), **list**, **load** (restore controls + re-validate),\n  **delete**, **clear**. All synchronous, on-device (AC-S1/S2/S3).\n- **No PII, no network** (AC-P2): the only stored data is car designs the user explicitly saves; a\n  visible \"clear my garage\" control exists.\n- A `schemaVersion` on each entry allows safe migration if `CarDesign` changes (relevant given the\n  build is deferred until the engine contract settles — A4).\n\n## 8. Privacy, offline & safety (PRD AC-P1/P2/P3)\n\n| Requirement | Implementation |\n| --- | --- |\n| No network at runtime | All assets same-origin & vendored; **no CDN, no fonts/analytics/embeds**; no `fetch`/`XHR`/`WebSocket` to any origin |\n| No PII / data collection | Only `localStorage` car designs; no accounts, no input fields for personal data, no telemetry |\n| Works offline | Service worker precaches the full static bundle; subsequent loads need no network |\n| Safe for children | Encouraging copy, no external links opened without intent; the `0004` leaderboard (the only network feature) is explicitly **not** here |\n\nCI/lint check: a test asserts the built bundle references **no off-origin URLs** (guards AC-P1\nagainst regressions).\n\n## 9. Accessibility (PRD AC-A1/A2/A3)\n\n- Native, labeled form controls (`<input type=range>`, toggles, buttons) with `<label>`/`aria-*`;\n  logical tab order; visible focus rings; **Race** reachable and operable by keyboard.\n- Results announced via an `aria-live` region so a screen reader reads the time + \"why\" after a race.\n- **WCAG-AA** contrast theme; **never color-only** — legal/over-limit, finish/DNF, and each loss bar\n  carry text + icon. Animation respects `prefers-reduced-motion` (offer a static end-state).\n- Responsive down to ~1024px; large targets for projector/Chromebook use.\n\n## 10. Dependencies & stack changes\n\n- **Python (runtime):** unchanged — `pinewood_derby` stays **stdlib-only**; `present.py` adds no\n  dependency. `pyproject` `dependencies = []` holds.\n- **New front-end toolchain (the stack expansion this feature introduces):**\n  - **TypeScript + Vite** build; **Pyodide** vendored as a static asset.\n  - **Playwright** (dev) for headless-browser UI tests; **Vitest** (or equivalent) for any pure TS\n    units.\n  - A **CI workflow** to build the engine wheel + the Vite bundle and deploy to GitHub Pages.\n- **Profile impact (flagged, not done here):** the profile's `framework`, `commands`\n  (build/test/run for the web app), `archetype` (desktop-app → web-app), deployment target, and\n  audience age (→ 12–17) all need a follow-up update for consistency. Tracked as a flag for the\n  synthesizer / a profile-update task (PRD §8).\n\n## 11. Risks & mitigations\n\n| Risk | Mitigation |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Engine contract still in flux** (`0001` building) — UI built against a moving target | **Defer build** until the contract stabilizes (A4); isolate all engine touchpoints behind `pyodide-bridge.ts` + the Python `present.py`/`to_dict`; version the garage JSON for migration |\n| **Pyodide first-load weight** (several MB) hurts the Chromebook/demo experience | Show a loading state (NFR); precache via service worker so it's a one-time cost; vendor + compress assets; lazy-load nothing the first race needs |\n| **Physics/units leaking to the kid** (jargon, Joules) | All translation in one pure module with a **banned-terms guard** shared by `test_present.py` and a UI text scan (AC-X3) |\n| **Priority order inverted in tips** (teaching wrong order) | The \"why\"/tips lookup is **reviewed, table-driven, priority-ordered**; a domain test asserts weight/placement & friction outrank aero across sample designs (AC-X4, rides engine AC-ED1) |\n| **Determinism breaks** (random seed, animation jitter) | UI pins `seed=FIXED_SEED` (A6); animation is a pure function of the returned trajectory; AC-R3 test races twice and asserts identical time/frames |\n| **Accidental third-party call** (font, CDN, analytics) creeps in | Same-origin-only policy + a build test asserting **no off-origin URLs** in the bundle (AC-P1) |\n| **Test stack expansion** beyond the profile's Python-only toolchain | Keep the **richest logic in pure Python** (`present.py`, `pytest`); limit browser tests to genuinely UI behavior; document the new commands for the profile update |\n| **Bigger UI surface than a TDD-friendly unit** | Push testable logic into `present.py` + control-domain mapping (unit-testable); reserve Playwright for a small set of end-to-end ACs (race, DNF, save/load, no-network, keyboard) |\n\n## 12. Test strategy\n\n- **Pure translation layer (`present.py`) — `uv run pytest`, the primary bar:**\n  - View-model mapping: ledger → ranked `LossBar`s largest-first (AC-X1); dominant-factor \"why\"\n    selection (AC-X2); legal/over-limit headline (AC-C3).\n  - **Non-finish classifier (AC-R4):** drive `present()` with **real `simulate()` output** (not\n    hand-built fixtures): an unstable design (`d_COM/L` below the cliff) → `outcome=\"tipped\"`,\n    `stopped_distance_frac == 0`, single-point trajectory, all-zero ledger; a stable-but-underpowered\n    design (e.g. a light ~1–2 oz car that stalls short) → `outcome=\"stalled\"`,\n    `0 < stopped_distance_frac < 1`, *non-crash* message. Assert the two never collapse into one and a\n    slow finisher (`outcome=\"finished\"`) is neither.\n  - **Banned-terms guard:** assert no jargon in any emitted string across a matrix of designs\n    (AC-X3).\n  - **Priority-order domain test:** across sample designs, weight/placement & friction produce the\n    largest surfaced losses/tips, aero the smallest (AC-X4).\n  - Determinism: `present(simulate(car, seed=S), car)` is stable (AC-R3, data side).\n  - **≥ 90% coverage** on `present.py` (PRD NFR).\n- **UI — Playwright (headless), one spec per UI AC:** default car loads & races (AC-C2/R1);\n  out-of-range/invalid input never throws (AC-C1); over-limit raceable + flagged (AC-C3); both\n  non-finish states render distinctly — `tipped` vs `stalled` (AC-R2/AC-R4); race-twice determinism\n  (AC-R3); save→reload→load→race (AC-S1/S2/S3); **no off-origin\n  network requests** via request interception (AC-P1); offline load after first visit (AC-P3);\n  keyboard-only loop + `aria-live` result (AC-A1); not-color-only / contrast (AC-A2).\n- **Engine untouched:** the `0001` suite continues to pass; a guard asserts no physics math lives\n  outside `pinewood_derby` (AC-G1).\n\n## 13. Traceability (AC → component)\n\n| Area | ACs | Primary component(s) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Controls → CarDesign | AC-C1, AC-C2, AC-C3 | `controls.ts`, `presets.ts`, `pyodide-bridge.ts` |\n| Race & animation | AC-R1, AC-R2, AC-R3, AC-R4 | `animator.ts`, `pyodide-bridge.ts`, `present.py` (non-finish classifier) |\n| Explanation / \"why\" | AC-X1, AC-X2, AC-X3, AC-X4 | `present.py`, `result-view.ts` |\n| Garage | AC-S1, AC-S2, AC-S3 | `garage.ts`, `present.py` (to_dict/from_dict) |\n| Privacy / offline / safety | AC-P1, AC-P2, AC-P3 | bundle policy, `sw.ts`, `garage.ts` |\n| Accessibility | AC-A1, AC-A2, AC-A3 | `a11y/`, `styles/`, `result-view.ts` |\n| Engine purity | AC-G1 | `present.py`, `pyodide-bridge.ts` |\n","numLines":296,"startLine":1,"totalLines":296}}}
