t_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":20070},\"output_tokens\":5,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"55f4d0f9-3f78-404c-9d9b-b1c51c035e71\",\"uuid\":\"8a04bd1f-e54a-4611-a25c-8129883cacdb\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CbfdvXkjYjTVYTEKsXADU\"}\n{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"commands_changed\",\"commands\":[{\"name\":\"author-requirements\",\"description\":\"Author a feature's PRD and TRD and render them to self-contained styled HTML files (PRD.html, TRD.html) that the dashboard and humans review. Maintains the feature's open-questions gate. Use during planning whenever creating or refining requirements. (project)\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"bootstrap-project\",\"description\":\"Create a new app (project) in the factory — interactively define it, write its profile.md from the template, scaffold its toolchain so the profile's commands run, and create its features/ dir. Use when starting a brand-new app. (project)\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"propose-feature\",\"description\":\"Capture a new feature idea as a proposed feature in the backlog (creates a schema-valid feature record with status=proposed). Use when, while planning or refining one feature, a distinct out-of-scope idea emerges that should become its own feature later. (project)\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"deep-research\",\"description\":\"Deep research harness — fan-out web searches, fetch sources, adversarially verify claims, synthesize a cited report. (dynamic workflow)\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"update-config\",\"description\":\"Use this skill to configure the Claude Code harness via settings.json. Automated behaviors (\\\"from now on when X\\\", \\\"each time X\\\", \\\"whenever X\\\", \\\"before/after X\\\") require hooks configured in settings.json - the harness executes these, not Claude, so memory/preferences cannot fulfill them. Also use for: permissions (\\\"allow X\\\", \\\"add permission\\\", \\\"move permission to\\\"), env vars (\\\"set X=Y\\\"), hook troubleshooting, or any changes to settings.json/settings.local.json files. Examples: \\\"allow npm commands\\\", \\\"add bq permission to global settings\\\", \\\"move permission to user settings\\\", \\\"set DEBUG=true\\\", \\\"when claude stops show X\\\". For simple settings like theme/model, suggest the /config command.\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"verify\",\"description\":\"Verify that a code change actually does what it's supposed to by running the app and observing behavior. Use when asked to verify a PR, confirm a fix works, test a change manually, check that a feature works, or validate local changes before pushing.\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"debug\",\"description\":\"Enable debug logging for this session and help diagnose issues\",\"argumentHint\":\"[issue description]\"},{\"name\":\"code-review\",\"description\":\"Review the current diff for correctness bugs and reuse/simplification/efficiency cleanups at the given effort level (low/medium: fewer, high-confidence findings; high→max: broader coverage, may include uncertain findings; ultra: deep multi-agent review in the cloud). Pass --comment to post findings as inline PR comments, or --fix to apply the findings to the working tree after the review.\",\"argumentHint\":\"[low|medium|high|xhigh|max|ultra] [--fix] [--comment] [<target>]\"},{\"name\":\"simplify\",\"description\":\"Review the changed code for reuse, simplification, efficiency, and altitude cleanups, then apply the fixes. Quality only — it does not hunt for bugs; use /code-review for that.\",\"argumentHint\":\"[<target>]\"},{\"name\":\"batch\",\"description\":\"Research and plan a large-scale change, then execute it in parallel across 5–30 isolated worktree agents that each open a PR.\",\"argumentHint\":\"<instruction>\"},{\"name\":\"fewer-permission-prompts\",\"description\":\"Scan your transcripts for common read-only Bash and MCP tool calls, then add a prioritized allowlist to project .claude/settings.json to reduce permission prompts.\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"loop\",\"description\":\"Run a prompt or slash command on a recurring interval (e.g. /loop 5m /foo). Omit the interval to let the model self-pace.\",\"argumentHint\":\"[interval] [prompt]\",\"aliases\":[\"proactive\"]},{\"name\":\"schedule\",\"description\":\"Create, update, list, or run scheduled remote agents (routines) that execute on a cron schedule.\",\"argumentHint\":\"\",\"aliases\":[\"routines\"]},{\"name\":\"claude-api\",\"description\":\"Build, debug, and optimize Claude API / Anthropic SDK apps. Apps built with this skill should include prompt caching. Also handles migrating existing Claude API code between Claude model versions (4.5 → 4.6, 4.6 → 4.7, retired-model replacements).\\nTRIGGER when: code imports `anthropic`/`@anthropic-ai/sdk`; user asks for the Claude API, Anthropic SDK, or Managed Agents; user adds/modifies/tunes a Claude feature (caching, thinking, compaction, tool use, batch, files, citations, memory) or model (Opus/Sonnet/Haiku) in a file; questions about prompt caching / cache hit rate in an Anthropic SDK project.\\nSKIP: file imports `openai`/other-provider SDK, filename like `*-openai.py`/`*-generic.py`, provider-neutral code, general programming/ML.\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"run\",\"description\":\"Launch and drive this project's app to see a change working. Use when asked to run, start, or screenshot the app, or to confirm a change works in the real app (not just tests). First looks for a project skill that already covers launching the app; otherwise falls back to built-in patterns per project type (CLI, server, TUI, Electron, browser-driven, library).\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"run-skill-generator\",\"description\":\"Author or improve the run-<unit> skill — a per-project skill that tells agents how to build, launch, and drive this project's app. Use when the user asks to set up the project, get it running, write run instructions, or verify build/run steps work from a clean environment.\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"clear\",\"description\":\"Start a new session with empty context; previous session stays on disk (resumable with /resume)\",\"argumentHint\":\"[name]\",\"aliases\":[\"reset\",\"new\"]},{\"name\":\"compact\",\"description\":\"Free up context by summarizing the conversation so far\",\"argumentHint\":\"<optional custom summarization instructions>\"},{\"name\":\"context\",\"description\":\"Show current context usage\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"heapdump\",\"description\":\"Dump the JS heap to ~/Desktop\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"init\",\"description\":\"Initialize a new CLAUDE.md file with codebase documentation\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"reload-skills\",\"description\":\"Pick up skills added or changed on disk during this session\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"review\",\"description\":\"Review a pull request\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"security-review\",\"description\":\"Complete a security review of the pending changes on the current branch\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"usage-credits\",\"description\":\"Configure usage credits to keep working when you hit a limit\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"extra-usage\",\"description\":\"Renamed to /usage-credits\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"usage\",\"description\":\"Show the total cost and duration of the current session\",\"argumentHint\":\"\",\"aliases\":[\"cost\",\"stats\"]},{\"name\":\"insights\",\"description\":\"Generate a report analyzing your Claude Code sessions\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"goal\",\"description\":\"Set a goal — keep working until the condition is met\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"team-onboarding\",\"description\":\"Help teammates ramp on Claude Code with a guide from your usage\",\"argumentHint\":\"\"}],\"uuid\":\"07c3280a-3009-42ba-91a5-f0e572c4f1d5\",\"session_id\":\"55f4d0f9-3f78-404c-9d9b-b1c51c035e71\"}\n{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01TfhiXSNmep96VgLQqDwnE7\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\texport const meta = {\\n2\\t  name: 'build-loop',\\n3\\t  description: 'Deterministic TDD build loop for one approved feature: PO decompose -> (QA red -> dev green -> QA validate -> adversarial review)* -> PO sign-off. Returns structured results for the run-record. Starts AFTER PRD/TRD approval; ends at the PO sign-off verdict (the human accept-gate happens in the main conversation).',\\n4\\t  phases: [\\n5\\t    { title: 'Decompose', detail: 'PO turns the approved PRD/TRD into a testable backlog' },\\n6\\t    { title: 'Build', detail: 'per work item: QA red -> dev green -> QA validate' },\\n7\\t    { title: 'Review', detail: 'adversarial review loop until clean or capped' },\\n8\\t    { title: 'Sign-off', detail: 'PO acceptance vs PRD/TRD' },\\n9\\t  ],\\n10\\t}\\n11\\t\\n12\\t// ── inputs (args) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\n13\\t// { app, feature, prdRef, trdRef, profileRef, gatesRef?, caps?, severityThreshold? }\\n14\\t// Refs are PATHS the agents READ themselves (the workflow runtime has no filesystem).\\n15\\tconst A = typeof args === 'string' ? JSON.parse(args || '{}') : (args || {})\\n16\\tif (!A.prdRef || !A.trdRef || !A.profileRef) {\\n17\\t  throw new Error('build-loop requires args.prdRef, args.trdRef, args.profileRef (paths the agents will read)')\\n18\\t}\\n19\\tconst GATES = A.gatesRef || 'agentic-sdlc/gates.md'\\n20\\tconst caps = Object.assign({ green: 6, adversarial: 3 }, A.caps || {})\\n21\\tconst SEV = { critical: 4, high: 3, medium: 2, low: 1 }\\n22\\tconst THRESHOLD = SEV[A.severityThreshold || 'high']\\n23\\tconst ctx =\\n24\\t  `App profile: ${A.profileRef}\\\\n` +\\n25\\t  `Approved PRD: ${A.prdRef}\\\\n` +\\n26\\t  `Approved TRD: ${A.trdRef}\\\\n` +\\n27\\t  `Gate criteria (your definition of done): ${GATES}\\\\n` +\\n28\\t  `Read these files yourself before acting.` +\\n29\\t  // Optional incremental-build scope: when set, prior work items are already built and\\n30\\t  // GREEN; the PO decomposes only the remaining acceptance criteria and no agent\\n31\\t  // rebuilds or weakens existing passing tests. Empty on a from-scratch build.\\n32\\t  (A.scopeNote ? `\\\\n\\\\nINCREMENTAL BUILD SCOPE — read and honor before acting:\\\\n${A.scopeNote}` : '')\\n33\\t\\n34\\t// ── gate verdict schemas (mirror gates.md) ───────────────────────────────────\\n35\\tconst BACKLOG = { type: 'object', required: ['work_items'], properties: { work_items: { type: 'array', items: {\\n36\\t  type: 'object', required: ['id', 'title', 'acceptance_criteria'], properties: {\\n37\\t    id: { type: 'string' }, title: { type: 'string' },\\n38\\t    acceptance_criteria: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },\\n39\\t    depends_on: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } } } } } } }\\n40\\t\\n41\\tconst RED = { type: 'object', required: ['red_confirmed', 'tests'], properties: {\\n42\\t  red_confirmed: { type: 'boolean' }, deterministic: { type: 'boolean' },\\n43\\t  tests: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['criterion', 'test_id', 'failing'], properties: {\\n44\\t    criterion: { type: 'string' }, test_id: { type: 'string' },\\n45\\t    failing: { type: 'boolean' }, fails_for_right_reason: { type: 'boolean' } } } },\\n46\\t  notes: { type: 'string' } } }\\n47\\t\\n48\\tconst GREEN = { type: 'object', required: ['green', 'tests_unmodified'], properties: {\\n49\\t  green: { type: 'boolean' }, lint_pass: { type: 'boolean' }, typecheck_pass: { type: 'boolean' },\\n50\\t  tests_unmodified: { type: 'boolean' }, summary: { type: 'string' } } }\\n51\\t\\n52\\tconst VALIDATE = { type: 'object', required: ['validated', 'criteria'], properties: {\\n53\\t  validated: { type: 'boolean' }, coverage: { type: 'number' },\\n54\\t  criteria: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['criterion', 'passing'], properties: {\\n55\\t    criterion: { type: 'string' }, covered_by: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },\\n56\\t    passing: { type: 'boolean' } } } },\\n57\\t  unmapped: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } } } }\\n58\\t\\n59\\tconst ADVERSARIAL = { type: 'object', required: ['findings'], properties: {\\n60\\t  findings: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['id', 'category', 'severity', 'reproducible'], properties: {\\n61\\t    id: { type: 'string' }, category: { type: 'string' },\\n62\\t    severity: { type: 'string', enum: ['critical', 'high', 'medium', 'low'] },\\n63\\t    description: { type: 'string' }, repro: { type: 'string' }, reproducible: { type: 'boolean' } } } },\\n64\\t  categories_checked: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } } } }\\n65\\t\\n66\\tconst SIGNOFF = { type: 'object', required: ['signed_off', 'criteria'], properties: {\\n67\\t  signed_off: { type: 'boolean' },\\n68\\t  criteria: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['criterion', 'met'], properties: {\\n69\\t    criterion: { type: 'string' }, met: { type: 'boolean' }, evidence: { type: 'string' } } } },\\n70\\t  unmet: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },\\n71\\t  nfr: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', properties: {\\n72\\t    name: { type: 'string' }, met: { type: 'boolean' }, evidence: { type: 'string' } } } } } }\\n73\\t\\n74\\t// ── helper: developer iterates to GREEN (capped) ─────────────────────────────\\n75\\tasync function devToGreen(item, intent, phaseName, startAttempt) {\\n76\\t  let attempts = startAttempt || 0\\n77\\t  let green = null\\n78\\t  while (attempts < caps.green) {\\n79\\t    attempts++\\n80\\t    green = await agent(\\n81\\t      `You are the Developer. ${intent}\\\\n${ctx}\\\\n` +\\n82\\t      `Work item: ${item.id} — ${item.title}\\\\n` +\\n83\\t      `Run the profile's test/lint/typecheck commands. NEVER modify, skip, or delete tests. ` +\\n84\\t      `Apply the Developer gate in ${GATES}. Attempt ${attempts}/${caps.green}.`,\\n85\\t      { agentType: 'developer', phase: phaseName, label: `dev:${item.id}#${attempts}`, schema: GREEN }\\n86\\t    )\\n87\\t    if (green && green.green && green.tests_unmodified) break\\n88\\t  }\\n89\\t  return { green, attempts }\\n90\\t}\\n91\\t\\n92\\t// ── 0. Decompose ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\n93\\tphase('Decompose')\\n94\\tconst backlog = await agent(\\n95\\t  `You are the Product Owner. ${ctx}\\\\n` +\\n96\\t  `Decompose the approved PRD/TRD into independently testable, vertically-sliced work items, each ` +\\n97\\t  `with acceptance criteria traceable to a PRD line. Apply the \\\"PO Decompose\\\" gate in ${GATES}.`,\\n98\\t  { agentType: 'product-owner', label: 'po:decompose', schema: BACKLOG }\\n99\\t)\\n100\\tconst items = backlog.work_items || []\\n101\\tlog(`Decomposed into ${items.length} work item(s)`)\\n102\\t\\n103\\t// ── 1–4. Build each item SEQUENTIALLY (shared mutable codebase → no parallel/worktree in v1) ──\\n104\\tconst results = []\\n105\\tfor (const item of items) {\\n106\\t  phase('Build')\\n107\\t  const red = await agent(\\n108\\t    `You are QA. ${ctx}\\\\nWork item: ${item.id} — ${item.title}\\\\n` +\\n109\\t    `Acceptance criteria:\\\\n- ${(item.acceptance_criteria || []).join('\\\\n- ')}\\\\n` +\\n110\\t    `Write failing tests for every criterion. Apply the \\\"QA Red\\\" gate in ${GATES} — confirm true RED.`,\\n111\\t    { agentType: 'qa', phase: 'Build', label: `qa-red:${item.id}`, schema: RED }\\n112\\t  )\\n113\\t\\n114\\t  let { green, attempts } = await devToGreen(item, 'Make the failing tests pass.', 'Build', 0)\\n115\\t\\n116\\t  const validate = await agent(\\n117\\t    `You are QA. ${ctx}\\\\nWork item: ${item.id} — ${item.title}\\\\n` +\\n118\\t    `Validate the implementation against the acceptance criteria. Apply the \\\"QA Validate\\\" gate in ${GATES}.`,\\n119\\t    { agentType: 'qa', phase: 'Build', label: `qa-validate:${item.id}`, schema: VALIDATE }\\n120\\t  )\\n121\\t\\n122\\t  // ── adversarial loop ──\\n123\\t  phase('Review')\\n124\\t  let iteration = 0\\n125\\t  let adv = null\\n126\\t  let escalated = false\\n127\\t  while (true) {\\n128\\t    adv = await agent(\\n129\\t      `You are the Adversarial Reviewer. ${ctx}\\\\nWork item: ${item.id} — ${item.title}\\\\n` +\\n130\\t      `Work the full coverage checklist in ${GATES} and try to break it. Findings must be reproducible. ` +\\n131\\t      `Review pass #${iteration}.`,\\n132\\t      { agentType: 'adversarial-reviewer', phase: 'Review', label: `adv:${item.id}#${iteration}`, schema: ADVERSARIAL }\\n133\\t    )\\n134\\t    const open = (adv.findings || []).filter(f => f.reproducible && SEV[f.severity] >= THRESHOLD)\\n135\\t    if (open.length === 0) break\\n136\\t    if (iteration >= caps.adversarial) {\\n137\\t      escalated = true\\n138\\t      log(`Adversarial cap (${caps.adversarial}) hit on ${item.id} with ${open.length} open finding(s) — escalating`)\\n139\\t      break\\n140\\t    }\\n141\\t    await agent(\\n142\\t      `You are QA. ${ctx}\\\\nWork item: ${item.id} — ${item.title}\\\\n` +\\n143\\t      `Write covering failing tests for these confirmed adversarial findings, then stop:\\\\n` +\\n144\\t      `${JSON.stringify(open, null, 2)}\\\\nApply the \\\"QA Red\\\" gate.`,\\n145\\t      { agentType: 'qa', phase: 'Review', label: `qa-edge:${item.id}#${iteration}`, schema: RED }\\n146\\t    )\\n147\\t    const fix = await devToGreen(item, 'fix: make the new edge-case tests pass without weakening any test.', 'Review', attempts)\\n148\\t    attempts = fix.attempts\\n149\\t    green = fix.green\\n150\\t    iteration++\\n151\\t  }\\n152\\t\\n153\\t  results.push({\\n154\\t    item, red, green, validate,\\n155\\t    adversarial: adv, adversarial_iterations: iteration,\\n156\\t    dev_attempts: attempts, escalated,\\n157\\t  })\\n158\\t}\\n159\\t\\n160\\t// ── 5. PO Sign-off (verdict returned to the main conversation for the human accept-gate) ──\\n161\\tphase('Sign-off')\\n162\\tconst signoff = await agent(\\n163\\t  `You are the Product Owner. ${ctx}\\\\n` +\\n164\\t  `Final sign-off: does the built feature meet EVERY PRD/TRD acceptance criterion and the profile NFRs, ` +\\n165\\t  `with evidence? Apply the \\\"PO Sign-off\\\" gate in ${GATES}. You are a protective gate — never relax the bar.`,\\n166\\t  { agentType: 'product-owner', label: 'po:signoff', schema: SIGNOFF }\\n167\\t)\\n168\\t\\n169\\treturn {\\n170\\t  app: A.app,\\n171\\t  feature: A.feature,\\n172\\t  backlog,\\n173\\t  results,\\n174\\t  signoff,\\n175\\t  escalated: results.some(r => r.escalated) || !signoff.signed_off,\\n176\\t}\\n177\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"55f4d0f9-3f78-404c-9d9b-b1c51c035e71\",\"uuid\":\"01a45c91-4af7-4f72-ad37-ce59c96062a4\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-03T03:44:24.282Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/ericburdett/Projects/agentic-sdlc/workflows/build-loop.mjs\",\"content\":\"export const meta = {\\n  name: 'build-loop',\\n  description: 'Deterministic TDD build loop for one approved feature: PO decompose -> (QA red -> dev green -> QA validate -> adversarial review)* -> PO sign-off. Returns structured results for the run-record. Starts AFTER PRD/TRD approval; ends at the PO sign-off verdict (the human accept-gate happens in the main conversation).',\\n  phases: [\\n    { title: 'Decompose', detail: 'PO turns the approved PRD/TRD into a testable backlog' },\\n    { title: 'Build', detail: 'per work item: QA red -> dev green -> QA validate' },\\n    { title: 'Review', detail: 'adversarial review loop until clean or capped' },\\n    { title: 'Sign-off', detail: 'PO acceptance vs PRD/TRD' },\\n  ],\\n}\\n\\n// ── inputs (args) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\n// { app, feature, prdRef, trdRef, profileRef, gatesRef?, caps?, severityThreshold? }\\n// Refs are PATHS the agents READ themselves (the workflow runtime has no filesystem).\\nconst A = typeof args === 'string' ? JSON.parse(args || '{}') : (args || {})\\nif (!A.prdRef || !A.trdRef || !A.profileRef) {\\n  throw new Error('build-loop requires args.prdRef, args.trdRef, args.profileRef (paths the agents will read)')\\n}\\nconst GATES = A.gatesRef || 'agentic-sdlc/gates.md'\\nconst caps = Object.assign({ green: 6, adversarial: 3 }, A.caps || {})\\nconst SEV = { critical: 4, high: 3, medium: 2, low: 1 }\\nconst THRESHOLD = SEV[A.severityThreshold || 'high']\\nconst ctx =\\n  `App profile: ${A.profileRef}\\\\n` +\\n  `Approved PRD: ${A.prdRef}\\\\n` +\\n  `Approved TRD: ${A.trdRef}\\\\n` +\\n  `Gate criteria (your definition of done): ${GATES}\\\\n` +\\n  `Read these files yourself before acting.` +\\n  // Optional incremental-build scope: when set, prior work items are already built and\\n  // GREEN; the PO decomposes only the remaining acceptance criteria and no agent\\n  // rebuilds or weakens existing passing tests. Empty on a from-scratch build.\\n  (A.scopeNote ? `\\\\n\\\\nINCREMENTAL BUILD SCOPE — read and honor before acting:\\\\n${A.scopeNote}` : '')\\n\\n// ── gate verdict schemas (mirror gates.md) ───────────────────────────────────\\nconst BACKLOG = { type: 'object', required: ['work_items'], properties: { work_items: { type: 'array', items: {\\n  type: 'object', required: ['id', 'title', 'acceptance_criteria'], properties: {\\n    id: { type: 'string' }, title: { type: 'string' },\\n    acceptance_criteria: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },\\n    depends_on: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } } } } } } }\\n\\nconst RED = { type: 'object', required: ['red_confirmed', 'tests'], properties: {\\n  red_confirmed: { type: 'boolean' }, deterministic: { type: 'boolean' },\\n  tests: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['criterion', 'test_id', 'failing'], properties: {\\n    criterion: { type: 'string' }, test_id: { type: 'string' },\\n    failing: { type: 'boolean' }, fails_for_right_reason: { type: 'boolean' } } } },\\n  notes: { type: 'string' } } }\\n\\nconst GREEN = { type: 'object', required: ['green', 'tests_unmodified'], properties: {\\n  green: { type: 'boolean' }, lint_pass: { type: 'boolean' }, typecheck_pass: { type: 'boolean' },\\n  tests_unmodified: { type: 'boolean' }, summary: { type: 'string' } } }\\n\\nconst VALIDATE = { type: 'object', required: ['validated', 'criteria'], properties: {\\n  validated: { type: 'boolean' }, coverage: { type: 'number' },\\n  criteria: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['criterion', 'passing'], properties: {\\n    criterion: { type: 'string' }, covered_by: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },\\n    passing: { type: 'boolean' } } } },\\n  unmapped: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } } } }\\n\\nconst ADVERSARIAL = { type: 'object', required: ['findings'], properties: {\\n  findings: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['id', 'category', 'severity', 'reproducible'], properties: {\\n    id: { type: 'string' }, category: { type: 'string' },\\n    severity: { type: 'string', enum: ['critical', 'high', 'medium', 'low'] },\\n    description: { type: 'string' }, repro: { type: 'string' }, reproducible: { type: 'boolean' } } } },\\n  categories_checked: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } } } }\\n\\nconst SIGNOFF = { type: 'object', required: ['signed_off', 'criteria'], properties: {\\n  signed_off: { type: 'boolean' },\\n  criteria: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['criterion', 'met'], properties: {\\n    criterion: { type: 'string' }, met: { type: 'boolean' }, evidence: { type: 'string' } } } },\\n  unmet: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },\\n  nfr: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', properties: {\\n    name: { type: 'string' }, met: { type: 'boolean' }, evidence: { type: 'string' } } } } } }\\n\\n// ── helper: developer iterates to GREEN (capped) ─────────────────────────────\\nasync function devToGreen(item, intent, phaseName, startAttempt) {\\n  let attempts = startAttempt || 0\\n  let green = null\\n  while (attempts < caps.green) {\\n    attempts++\\n    green = await agent(\\n      `You are the Developer. ${intent}\\\\n${ctx}\\\\n` +\\n      `Work item: ${item.id} — ${item.title}\\\\n` +\\n      `Run the profile's test/lint/typecheck commands. NEVER modify, skip, or delete tests. ` +\\n      `Apply the Developer gate in ${GATES}. Attempt ${attempts}/${caps.green}.`,\\n      { agentType: 'developer', phase: phaseName, label: `dev:${item.id}#${attempts}`, schema: GREEN }\\n    )\\n    if (green && green.green && green.tests_unmodified) bre","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/Users/ericburdett/.claude/projects/-Users-ericburdett-Projects/55f4d0f9-3f78-404c-9d9b-b1c51c035e71/tool-results/bfk7df290.txt","persistedOutputSize":207312}}
