{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_016wfkip3cVEKX9N6g2WXVH1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013vcJDkysqkXrwfmr5TR9Qz","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/ericburdett/.claude/projects/-Users-ericburdett-Projects/55f4d0f9-3f78-404c-9d9b-b1c51c035e71/subagents/workflows/wf_192cd4bd-629 && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,glob,os\npo=\"agent-afd052beb1b9ebcd8.jsonl\"\nitems=None\nfor line in open(po):\n    try: rec=json.loads(line)\n    except: continue\n    def walk(o):\n        global items\n        if isinstance(o,dict):\n            if o.get('type')=='tool_use' and 'work_items' in (o.get('input') or {}):\n                items=o['input']['work_items']\n            for v in o.values(): walk(v)\n        elif isinstance(o,list):\n            for v in o: walk(v)\n    walk(rec)\nprint(\"num work items:\",len(items) if items else None)\nfor i in items or []:\n    print(i.get('id'),'|',i.get('title'))\n    print('     ACs:',', '.join(i.get('acceptance_criteria',[])))\nPY","description":"Parse PO backlog from transcript"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1551,"cache_read_input_tokens":117423,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1551},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55f4d0f9-3f78-404c-9d9b-b1c51c035e71","uuid":"13a2ab09-dec5-4f8f-95f5-eb673619e482","request_id":"req_011CbgMFtDr1PUun6siRB1Gt"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013vcJDkysqkXrwfmr5TR9Qz","type":"tool_result","content":"num work items: 15\nWI01-PRESENT-VIEWMODEL | Pure translation layer: present() core view-model (finished-run mapping)\n     ACs: present.py exposes a pure function present(result: RaceResult, car: CarDesign) -> RaceView and to_json(view) -> dict, with frozen dataclasses (RaceView, LossBar, FramePoint); the module imports only from the pinewood_derby engine submodules (engine/car/result/track) and the stdlib, performs no DOM/I/O/network and computes no physics math (PRD AC-G1)., For a FINISHED run, present() sets finished=True, outcome='finished', and time_seconds equal to result.race_time_s (to display precision); seconds is the only numeric unit surfaced (PRD AC-R1 translation half, A7)., RaceView carries the trajectory as a tuple of FramePoint snapshots derived from result.trajectory (position/velocity/angle/t) for the animator to replay; no physics is recomputed (PRD AC-R1, AC-G1)., The translation layer is deterministic: present(simulate(car, seed=FIXED_SEED), car) returns an identical RaceView across repeated calls for the same design (PRD AC-R3 data side; NFR Determinism)., Unit-tested with `uv run pytest` against real simulate() output (not hand-built fixtures); present.py reaches >= 90% line coverage (PRD NFR 'Translation purity & coverage').\nWI02-PRESENT-BREAKDOWN | \"Where did your speed go?\" ranked energy breakdown (AC-X1)\n     ACs: For a finished run, RaceView.breakdown maps the engine ledger to LossBars: w_drag->'air', w_axle->'axle', w_rail->'rails', ke_rotational_final->'wheels', and final linear KE->'kept' (the 'speed you kept' bar), each with a plain-language label (PRD AC-X1, A8)., Bars are normalized to proportions of the energy actually delivered on the run (integrated w_gravity, not pe_initial) so the proportions sum to ~1.0 for both a finisher and a stalled car (TRD §4)., The breakdown is ranked largest-first (PRD AC-X1)., For a tipped run (all-zero ledger, w_gravity == 0) no breakdown bars are emitted, guarding against divide-by-zero; the tip's story is the headline, not a loss chart (TRD §4)., Covered by pytest unit tests driven by real simulate() output across multiple designs; contributes to the >= 90% present.py coverage bar (PRD NFR).\nWI03-PRESENT-WHY-PRIORITY | Dominant-factor \"why\" + tips, priority-order preserving (AC-X2, AC-X4)\n     ACs: RaceView.why names the dominant factor for the run in plain language and ties it to a real building principle via a reviewed table-driven lookup (axle->polish & graphite; rails->fix alignment/rail-ride; air->smoother/lower body; wheels->lighter/truer wheels; plus weight/placement coaching from legal_weight and car.com_ahead_of_rear_axle) (PRD AC-X2)., The 'why' selects the largest *loss* bar (excluding the 'kept' bar) as the dominant factor (TRD §4)., RaceView.tips holds 1-3 next-step suggestions ordered by the engine's real priority order; across sample designs, improving weight/placement and friction yields the largest surfaced gains and aerodynamics the smallest, and tips never advise aero over weight/friction (PRD AC-X4, rides engine AC-ED1)., A priority-order domain test asserts, across a matrix of sample designs, that the surfaced ranking/why never inverts the engine ordering (PRD AC-X4; TRD §12 priority-order domain test)., Covered by pytest unit tests; contributes to the >= 90% present.py coverage bar.\nWI04-PRESENT-NOJARGON | Banned-terms guard: no jargon in any emitted string (AC-X3)\n     ACs: No technical unit or term (Joules, Newtons, coefficient, m/s2, C_d, mu/µ, 'moment of inertia', 'normal force', and the rest of an agreed banned-term list) appears in any string field of any RaceView (headline, why, tips, bar labels) across a matrix of designs (finished, tipped, stalled, legal, over-limit) (PRD AC-X3)., A reusable banned-terms checker is exposed so the same list backs both this pytest guard and the later UI text scan (TRD §11 'banned-terms guard shared by test_present.py and a UI text scan')., The guard is a pytest test that fails if any new emitted string introduces a banned term.\nWI05-PRESENT-DNF-CLASSIFIER | Non-finish disambiguation: tipped vs stalled (AC-R4, AC-R2 data side)\n     ACs: For any engine outcome=DNF, present() sets finished=False and time_seconds=None and classifies the run into outcome='tipped' or outcome='stalled' from the trajectory + ledger only (no new physics) (PRD AC-R4, AC-R2; AC-G1)., A run with a single at-rest trajectory point at position 0 and an all-zero work ledger is classified 'tipped' with stopped_distance_frac=0.0 (driven by an unstable design where d_COM/L is below the stability cliff) (PRD AC-R4; engine confirms len(trajectory)==1, position==0, w_gravity==w_drag==w_axle==w_rail==0)., A run with a real multi-point trajectory whose last position satisfies 0 < position < track_length (= ramp_length + flat_length) and finish_velocity ~ 0 is classified 'stalled' with stopped_distance_frac = last_position/track_length in (0,1) (driven by a stable-but-underpowered ~1-2 oz design) (PRD AC-R4)., normal_forces is NOT used as the discriminator (it is a single static front/rear pair, front = M*g*(d_COM/L) >= 0 always) (PRD AC-R4 note; engine confirmed)., Each non-finish gets the matching kid-language, encouraging headline and a different correct 'why' (tipped: wobble/weight-too-far-back; stalled: ran out of speed/too much friction); a slow-but-stable car is never labeled a crash (PRD AC-R4, AC-R2)., A finished run is classified neither tipped nor stalled; tipped and stalled never collapse into one outcome. Tested via real simulate() output for an unstable design, an underpowered design, and a finisher; contributes to >= 90% present.py coverage (TRD §12).\nWI06-PRESENT-GARAGE-SERDE | CarDesign serialize/deserialize for the garage (versioned JSON, AC-S2 data side)\n     ACs: A pure to_dict(CarDesign)->dict and from_dict(dict)->CarDesign (in present.py or a sibling helper) round-trips every control field of a CarDesign losslessly: mass, com_ahead_of_rear_axle, wheelbase, wheels (count_touching, wheel_mass, outer/inner/axle radius), body, axle, alignment (PRD AC-S2; TRD §5/§7)., Each serialized entry carries a schemaVersion so a later CarDesign change can be migrated (TRD §7, PRD A4)., from_dict re-validates through CarDesign construction so a malformed/illegal stored design raises ValueError (caught upstream) rather than producing an invalid object (TRD §5)., Reconstructing a design from its serialized form and racing it reproduces the original design's time (with the fixed seed) (PRD AC-S2, AC-R3 data side)., Covered by pytest unit tests; contributes to >= 90% present.py coverage.\nWI07-BRIDGE-BOOT | Pyodide bridge: load vendored runtime + engine, typed call wrappers (foundation)\n     ACs: pyodide-bridge.ts loads the vendored same-origin Pyodide runtime and the pinewood_derby package (wheel or source) with no CDN/off-origin fetch, and exposes typed wrappers: buildCar(controlState)->CarDesign, race(car)->RaceView(JSON), plus garage serialize/deserialize wrappers (TRD §5)., race(car) calls simulate(car, seed=FIXED_SEED) then present(...) and returns a plain JSON view-model with no lingering PyProxy objects (PRD AC-R3, A6; TRD §5)., buildCar constructs the CarDesign in Python so the engine's own validation is the single source of truth; a Python ValueError is caught and returned as a surfaceable inline message, never a thrown stack trace (PRD AC-C1; TRD §5)., A loading state is exposed until Pyodide + engine are ready (PRD NFR 'Performance - load': usable within a few seconds with a loading indicator)., Verified by a Playwright headless-browser test that boots the app and confirms the bridge is ready and a race round-trips to a JSON view-model.\nWI08-UI-CONTROLS | Builder controls -> CarDesign with default car and live legal-weight (AC-C1, AC-C2, AC-C3)\n     ACs: Controls exist for all six engine levers + weight: weight (M), weight placement (d_COM), wheels (3/4 touching, light/standard), axle prep (polished+graphite <-> unprepared), body shape (wedge <-> block), alignment (rail-rider <-> straight); each maps to its CarDesign field (PRD §5; AC-C1)., Control domains pre-constrain inputs to the engine's valid bounds AND the Python validation is the backstop: the UI cannot submit a design the engine would reject; out-of-range or invalid combinations (e.g. wheels out-massing the car) are prevented or shown as an inline message, never an uncaught exception or stack trace (PRD AC-C1; TRD §5 two-layer guard)., On first open a legal, finishing default car is loaded and is immediately raceable (PRD AC-C2; presets.ts)., The displayed weight updates live and shows legal (<= 5.0 oz) vs over-limit status; an over-limit car is still raceable (rule shown, not enforced by physics), consistent with RaceView.legal_weight (PRD AC-C3)., Verified by Playwright tests: default car loads and races; a deliberately invalid/out-of-range input never throws and surfaces an inline message; an over-limit car is flagged yet raceable (TRD §12).\nWI09-UI-RACE-ANIMATION | Race + canvas trajectory animation for finishers (AC-R1, AC-R3 animation side)\n     ACs: Pressing Race runs simulate() on the current design and animates the car along the returned trajectory on a 2-D side-view <canvas> of STANDARD_TRACK (ramp -> transition -> flat) from start to finish; a finishing car visibly reaches the finish line (PRD AC-R1)., The displayed race time equals the engine's race_time_s to display precision, with a running clock during the animation (PRD AC-R1)., Animation is a pure function of the returned trajectory: racing the same design twice yields the same time and the same animation (the UI pins seed=FIXED_SEED) (PRD AC-R3; NFR Determinism)., Animation uses requestAnimationFrame and runs at >= 30 fps after warm-up; a race result renders within ~100 ms of pressing Race (PRD NFR 'Performance - race')., Verified by Playwright: a finisher animates to the finish line, the shown time matches the engine value, and a race-twice test asserts identical time and frames (TRD §12).\nWI10-UI-RESULT-PANEL | Result & \"why\" panel: time, ranked breakdown, principle-based why (AC-X1, AC-X2, AC-X3, AC-X4 surfaced)\n     ACs: After a finished race the result panel shows the time and the 'where did your speed go?' breakdown rendered largest-first from RaceView.breakdown (air/axle/rails/wheels/kept) (PRD AC-X1)., The panel shows the one-line 'why' naming the dominant factor tied to a real principle (PRD AC-X2) and surfaces tips in priority order, never inverting the engine ordering (PRD AC-X4)., A UI text scan over all rendered strings finds no banned jargon term, using the shared banned-terms list (PRD AC-X3; TRD §11)., The panel faithfully surfaces the present.py view-model and adds no physics of its own (PRD AC-G1)., Verified by Playwright: a finished race renders the time, a ranked breakdown, and a 'why'; an automated rendered-string scan asserts no banned terms.\nWI11-UI-NONFINISH-RENDER | Distinct non-finish rendering: stalled coast-to-halt vs tipped wobble-at-line (AC-R2, AC-R4 surfaced)\n     ACs: A non-finishing design shows a clear, encouraging 'here is what happened - here is why' state with no numeric time and never an error dialog (PRD AC-R2)., A 'stalled' car (real multi-point trajectory) animates its real run and coasts to a visible halt short of the finish line, with no crash visuals (PRD AC-R2, AC-R4; TRD §6)., A 'tipped' car (single at-rest start point) never leaves the start line and shows a distinct wobble-at-the-line state rather than a mid-track animation (PRD AC-R2, AC-R4; TRD §6)., Non-finisher playback scales off the trajectory's own last t (not race_time_s, which is None) and caps/compresses a long stall trajectory to a few legible seconds; a tipped run shows the wobble state with no timeline to scale (TRD §6)., The two non-finish stories render distinctly and a slow-but-stable car is never shown as a crash (PRD AC-R4). Verified by separate Playwright specs driving a tipped design and a stalled design.\nWI12-UI-GARAGE | Local garage: name/save/list/load/delete via localStorage (AC-S1, AC-S2, AC-S3)\n     ACs: The current design can be named and saved to localStorage (single namespace, e.g. pds.garage.v1) and persists across a reload (PRD AC-S1; TRD §7)., Saved designs are listed; loading one restores every control to the saved values, and racing the loaded design reproduces its time with the fixed seed (PRD AC-S2)., A saved design can be deleted and the garage cleared via a visible control; the only persisted data is car designs, and nothing is sent off-device (PRD AC-S3; AC-P2)., Load reconstructs and re-validates the stored design through the bridge serde so a corrupt/illegal entry surfaces gracefully, never an uncaught exception (TRD §5/§7)., Verified by a Playwright save -> reload -> load -> race flow asserting persistence, full control restoration, and reproduced time, plus a delete/clear assertion (TRD §12).\nWI13-OFFLINE-NONETWORK | Same-origin assets, service-worker offline, no runtime network (AC-P1, AC-P2, AC-P3)\n     ACs: After initial asset load the app makes no network requests: no third-party CDNs, no analytics, no telemetry; all assets (Pyodide runtime + engine + fonts/styles) are same-origin and vendored (PRD AC-P1)., A build/CI check asserts the built bundle references no off-origin URLs, guarding AC-P1 against regression (TRD §8)., No personal data is collected or transmitted; the only persisted data is local car designs in browser storage; no accounts, no PII input fields (PRD AC-P2)., A service worker precaches the full static bundle (HTML/JS/CSS/Pyodide/engine) and the app works offline after the first load; the SW makes no network fetches of its own (PRD AC-P3; TRD §2/§8)., Verified by Playwright: request interception confirms zero off-origin requests during a full race after warm-up (AC-P1), and an offline-after-first-load test confirms the app loads and races with the network disabled (AC-P3).\nWI14-ACCESSIBILITY | Accessibility & demo-ready presentation: keyboard, WCAG-AA, not-color-only, responsive (AC-A1, AC-A2, AC-A3)\n     ACs: All controls and Race are keyboard-operable and labeled (native labeled form controls, aria-*), with a logical focus order and visible focus; a full configure -> race -> read-result loop is possible without a mouse, and the result (time + why) is announced via an aria-live region (PRD AC-A1; TRD §9)., Color is never the sole signal: legal/over-limit, finish/DNF, and each loss bar carry text/icon labels in addition to color; kid-facing text and controls meet WCAG-AA contrast (PRD AC-A2)., The layout is legible on a projector and a Chromebook: responsive to ~1024px wide with large, distinct touch/click targets; animation respects prefers-reduced-motion with a static end-state offered (PRD AC-A3; TRD §9)., Reading level and tone of kid-facing copy are tuned to ~12 yet legible for 17-year-olds (PRD §1, A2)., Verified by Playwright: a keyboard-only configure->race->read loop succeeds with aria-live result, and an automated check confirms non-color signals (text/icon) on legal/over-limit, finish/DNF, and loss bars (TRD §12).\nWI15-ENGINE-PURITY-GUARD | Engine-purity guard: front-end adds no physics, consumes public API unchanged (AC-G1)\n     ACs: The front-end consumes the engine's public API (simulate, CarDesign, Track, RaceResult) unchanged and adds no physics; present.py and the bridge compute only presentation (PRD AC-G1)., A guard test asserts no force/integration/physics math lives outside the pinewood_derby package (TRD §12 'no physics math outside the engine package')., The existing 0001 engine pytest suite continues to pass unmodified, and pinewood_derby stays stdlib-only (pyproject dependencies = []) (TRD §10)., Machine-checked: `uv run pytest`, `uv run ruff check .`, and `uv run mypy .` (strict) all pass for the Python side including present.py (profile commands).\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/ericburdett/Projects","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55f4d0f9-3f78-404c-9d9b-b1c51c035e71","uuid":"797bc3c6-d735-4044-8745-1055c7f8faf4","timestamp":"2026-06-03T12:46:29.914Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"num work items: 15\nWI01-PRESENT-VIEWMODEL | Pure translation layer: present() core view-model (finished-run mapping)\n     ACs: present.py exposes a pure function present(result: RaceResult, car: CarDesign) -> RaceView and to_json(view) -> dict, with frozen dataclasses (RaceView, LossBar, FramePoint); the module imports only from the pinewood_derby engine submodules (engine/car/result/track) and the stdlib, performs no DOM/I/O/network and computes no physics math (PRD AC-G1)., For a FINISHED run, present() sets finished=True, outcome='finished', and time_seconds equal to result.race_time_s (to display precision); seconds is the only numeric unit surfaced (PRD AC-R1 translation half, A7)., RaceView carries the trajectory as a tuple of FramePoint snapshots derived from result.trajectory (position/velocity/angle/t) for the animator to replay; no physics is recomputed (PRD AC-R1, AC-G1)., The translation layer is deterministic: present(simulate(car, seed=FIXED_SEED), car) returns an identical RaceView across repeated calls for the same design (PRD AC-R3 data side; NFR Determinism)., Unit-tested with `uv run pytest` against real simulate() output (not hand-built fixtures); present.py reaches >= 90% line coverage (PRD NFR 'Translation purity & coverage').\nWI02-PRESENT-BREAKDOWN | \"Where did your speed go?\" ranked energy breakdown (AC-X1)\n     ACs: For a finished run, RaceView.breakdown maps the engine ledger to LossBars: w_drag->'air', w_axle->'axle', w_rail->'rails', ke_rotational_final->'wheels', and final linear KE->'kept' (the 'speed you kept' bar), each with a plain-language label (PRD AC-X1, A8)., Bars are normalized to proportions of the energy actually delivered on the run (integrated w_gravity, not pe_initial) so the proportions sum to ~1.0 for both a finisher and a stalled car (TRD §4)., The breakdown is ranked largest-first (PRD AC-X1)., For a tipped run (all-zero ledger, w_gravity == 0) no breakdown bars are emitted, guarding against divide-by-zero; the tip's story is the headline, not a loss chart (TRD §4)., Covered by pytest unit tests driven by real simulate() output across multiple designs; contributes to the >= 90% present.py coverage bar (PRD NFR).\nWI03-PRESENT-WHY-PRIORITY | Dominant-factor \"why\" + tips, priority-order preserving (AC-X2, AC-X4)\n     ACs: RaceView.why names the dominant factor for the run in plain language and ties it to a real building principle via a reviewed table-driven lookup (axle->polish & graphite; rails->fix alignment/rail-ride; air->smoother/lower body; wheels->lighter/truer wheels; plus weight/placement coaching from legal_weight and car.com_ahead_of_rear_axle) (PRD AC-X2)., The 'why' selects the largest *loss* bar (excluding the 'kept' bar) as the dominant factor (TRD §4)., RaceView.tips holds 1-3 next-step suggestions ordered by the engine's real priority order; across sample designs, improving weight/placement and friction yields the largest surfaced gains and aerodynamics the smallest, and tips never advise aero over weight/friction (PRD AC-X4, rides engine AC-ED1)., A priority-order domain test asserts, across a matrix of sample designs, that the surfaced ranking/why never inverts the engine ordering (PRD AC-X4; TRD §12 priority-order domain test)., Covered by pytest unit tests; contributes to the >= 90% present.py coverage bar.\nWI04-PRESENT-NOJARGON | Banned-terms guard: no jargon in any emitted string (AC-X3)\n     ACs: No technical unit or term (Joules, Newtons, coefficient, m/s2, C_d, mu/µ, 'moment of inertia', 'normal force', and the rest of an agreed banned-term list) appears in any string field of any RaceView (headline, why, tips, bar labels) across a matrix of designs (finished, tipped, stalled, legal, over-limit) (PRD AC-X3)., A reusable banned-terms checker is exposed so the same list backs both this pytest guard and the later UI text scan (TRD §11 'banned-terms guard shared by test_present.py and a UI text scan')., The guard is a pytest test that fails if any new emitted string introduces a banned term.\nWI05-PRESENT-DNF-CLASSIFIER | Non-finish disambiguation: tipped vs stalled (AC-R4, AC-R2 data side)\n     ACs: For any engine outcome=DNF, present() sets finished=False and time_seconds=None and classifies the run into outcome='tipped' or outcome='stalled' from the trajectory + ledger only (no new physics) (PRD AC-R4, AC-R2; AC-G1)., A run with a single at-rest trajectory point at position 0 and an all-zero work ledger is classified 'tipped' with stopped_distance_frac=0.0 (driven by an unstable design where d_COM/L is below the stability cliff) (PRD AC-R4; engine confirms len(trajectory)==1, position==0, w_gravity==w_drag==w_axle==w_rail==0)., A run with a real multi-point trajectory whose last position satisfies 0 < position < track_length (= ramp_length + flat_length) and finish_velocity ~ 0 is classified 'stalled' with stopped_distance_frac = last_position/track_length in (0,1) (driven by a stable-but-underpowered ~1-2 oz design) (PRD AC-R4)., normal_forces is NOT used as the discriminator (it is a single static front/rear pair, front = M*g*(d_COM/L) >= 0 always) (PRD AC-R4 note; engine confirmed)., Each non-finish gets the matching kid-language, encouraging headline and a different correct 'why' (tipped: wobble/weight-too-far-back; stalled: ran out of speed/too much friction); a slow-but-stable car is never labeled a crash (PRD AC-R4, AC-R2)., A finished run is classified neither tipped nor stalled; tipped and stalled never collapse into one outcome. Tested via real simulate() output for an unstable design, an underpowered design, and a finisher; contributes to >= 90% present.py coverage (TRD §12).\nWI06-PRESENT-GARAGE-SERDE | CarDesign serialize/deserialize for the garage (versioned JSON, AC-S2 data side)\n     ACs: A pure to_dict(CarDesign)->dict and from_dict(dict)->CarDesign (in present.py or a sibling helper) round-trips every control field of a CarDesign losslessly: mass, com_ahead_of_rear_axle, wheelbase, wheels (count_touching, wheel_mass, outer/inner/axle radius), body, axle, alignment (PRD AC-S2; TRD §5/§7)., Each serialized entry carries a schemaVersion so a later CarDesign change can be migrated (TRD §7, PRD A4)., from_dict re-validates through CarDesign construction so a malformed/illegal stored design raises ValueError (caught upstream) rather than producing an invalid object (TRD §5)., Reconstructing a design from its serialized form and racing it reproduces the original design's time (with the fixed seed) (PRD AC-S2, AC-R3 data side)., Covered by pytest unit tests; contributes to >= 90% present.py coverage.\nWI07-BRIDGE-BOOT | Pyodide bridge: load vendored runtime + engine, typed call wrappers (foundation)\n     ACs: pyodide-bridge.ts loads the vendored same-origin Pyodide runtime and the pinewood_derby package (wheel or source) with no CDN/off-origin fetch, and exposes typed wrappers: buildCar(controlState)->CarDesign, race(car)->RaceView(JSON), plus garage serialize/deserialize wrappers (TRD §5)., race(car) calls simulate(car, seed=FIXED_SEED) then present(...) and returns a plain JSON view-model with no lingering PyProxy objects (PRD AC-R3, A6; TRD §5)., buildCar constructs the CarDesign in Python so the engine's own validation is the single source of truth; a Python ValueError is caught and returned as a surfaceable inline message, never a thrown stack trace (PRD AC-C1; TRD §5)., A loading state is exposed until Pyodide + engine are ready (PRD NFR 'Performance - load': usable within a few seconds with a loading indicator)., Verified by a Playwright headless-browser test that boots the app and confirms the bridge is ready and a race round-trips to a JSON view-model.\nWI08-UI-CONTROLS | Builder controls -> CarDesign with default car and live legal-weight (AC-C1, AC-C2, AC-C3)\n     ACs: Controls exist for all six engine levers + weight: weight (M), weight placement (d_COM), wheels (3/4 touching, light/standard), axle prep (polished+graphite <-> unprepared), body shape (wedge <-> block), alignment (rail-rider <-> straight); each maps to its CarDesign field (PRD §5; AC-C1)., Control domains pre-constrain inputs to the engine's valid bounds AND the Python validation is the backstop: the UI cannot submit a design the engine would reject; out-of-range or invalid combinations (e.g. wheels out-massing the car) are prevented or shown as an inline message, never an uncaught exception or stack trace (PRD AC-C1; TRD §5 two-layer guard)., On first open a legal, finishing default car is loaded and is immediately raceable (PRD AC-C2; presets.ts)., The displayed weight updates live and shows legal (<= 5.0 oz) vs over-limit status; an over-limit car is still raceable (rule shown, not enforced by physics), consistent with RaceView.legal_weight (PRD AC-C3)., Verified by Playwright tests: default car loads and races; a deliberately invalid/out-of-range input never throws and surfaces an inline message; an over-limit car is flagged yet raceable (TRD §12).\nWI09-UI-RACE-ANIMATION | Race + canvas trajectory animation for finishers (AC-R1, AC-R3 animation side)\n     ACs: Pressing Race runs simulate() on the current design and animates the car along the returned trajectory on a 2-D side-view <canvas> of STANDARD_TRACK (ramp -> transition -> flat) from start to finish; a finishing car visibly reaches the finish line (PRD AC-R1)., The displayed race time equals the engine's race_time_s to display precision, with a running clock during the animation (PRD AC-R1)., Animation is a pure function of the returned trajectory: racing the same design twice yields the same time and the same animation (the UI pins seed=FIXED_SEED) (PRD AC-R3; NFR Determinism)., Animation uses requestAnimationFrame and runs at >= 30 fps after warm-up; a race result renders within ~100 ms of pressing Race (PRD NFR 'Performance - race')., Verified by Playwright: a finisher animates to the finish line, the shown time matches the engine value, and a race-twice test asserts identical time and frames (TRD §12).\nWI10-UI-RESULT-PANEL | Result & \"why\" panel: time, ranked breakdown, principle-based why (AC-X1, AC-X2, AC-X3, AC-X4 surfaced)\n     ACs: After a finished race the result panel shows the time and the 'where did your speed go?' breakdown rendered largest-first from RaceView.breakdown (air/axle/rails/wheels/kept) (PRD AC-X1)., The panel shows the one-line 'why' naming the dominant factor tied to a real principle (PRD AC-X2) and surfaces tips in priority order, never inverting the engine ordering (PRD AC-X4)., A UI text scan over all rendered strings finds no banned jargon term, using the shared banned-terms list (PRD AC-X3; TRD §11)., The panel faithfully surfaces the present.py view-model and adds no physics of its own (PRD AC-G1)., Verified by Playwright: a finished race renders the time, a ranked breakdown, and a 'why'; an automated rendered-string scan asserts no banned terms.\nWI11-UI-NONFINISH-RENDER | Distinct non-finish rendering: stalled coast-to-halt vs tipped wobble-at-line (AC-R2, AC-R4 surfaced)\n     ACs: A non-finishing design shows a clear, encouraging 'here is what happened - here is why' state with no numeric time and never an error dialog (PRD AC-R2)., A 'stalled' car (real multi-point trajectory) animates its real run and coasts to a visible halt short of the finish line, with no crash visuals (PRD AC-R2, AC-R4; TRD §6)., A 'tipped' car (single at-rest start point) never leaves the start line and shows a distinct wobble-at-the-line state rather than a mid-track animation (PRD AC-R2, AC-R4; TRD §6)., Non-finisher playback scales off the trajectory's own last t (not race_time_s, which is None) and caps/compresses a long stall trajectory to a few legible seconds; a tipped run shows the wobble state with no timeline to scale (TRD §6)., The two non-finish stories render distinctly and a slow-but-stable car is never shown as a crash (PRD AC-R4). Verified by separate Playwright specs driving a tipped design and a stalled design.\nWI12-UI-GARAGE | Local garage: name/save/list/load/delete via localStorage (AC-S1, AC-S2, AC-S3)\n     ACs: The current design can be named and saved to localStorage (single namespace, e.g. pds.garage.v1) and persists across a reload (PRD AC-S1; TRD §7)., Saved designs are listed; loading one restores every control to the saved values, and racing the loaded design reproduces its time with the fixed seed (PRD AC-S2)., A saved design can be deleted and the garage cleared via a visible control; the only persisted data is car designs, and nothing is sent off-device (PRD AC-S3; AC-P2)., Load reconstructs and re-validates the stored design through the bridge serde so a corrupt/illegal entry surfaces gracefully, never an uncaught exception (TRD §5/§7)., Verified by a Playwright save -> reload -> load -> race flow asserting persistence, full control restoration, and reproduced time, plus a delete/clear assertion (TRD §12).\nWI13-OFFLINE-NONETWORK | Same-origin assets, service-worker offline, no runtime network (AC-P1, AC-P2, AC-P3)\n     ACs: After initial asset load the app makes no network requests: no third-party CDNs, no analytics, no telemetry; all assets (Pyodide runtime + engine + fonts/styles) are same-origin and vendored (PRD AC-P1)., A build/CI check asserts the built bundle references no off-origin URLs, guarding AC-P1 against regression (TRD §8)., No personal data is collected or transmitted; the only persisted data is local car designs in browser storage; no accounts, no PII input fields (PRD AC-P2)., A service worker precaches the full static bundle (HTML/JS/CSS/Pyodide/engine) and the app works offline after the first load; the SW makes no network fetches