{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01JSLL1TkKvjmgRY6ccXuZJM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Run-record is schema-valid. Now the human-facing escalation summary (mirroring the 0001 precedent's `ESCALATION.md`)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":393,"cache_read_input_tokens":141287,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":393},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55f4d0f9-3f78-404c-9d9b-b1c51c035e71","uuid":"d9589c57-b9e3-4621-b4c6-8c9c239d816c","request_id":"req_011CbgMWNfGR7NdxZgJVJzjo"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01JSLL1TkKvjmgRY6ccXuZJM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QAtnMA7MMW5UckYbbcYGe6","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ericburdett/Projects/agentic-sdlc/apps/pinewood-derby-sim/features/0003-web-front-end/ESCALATION.md","content":"# 0003-web-front-end — ESCALATION\n\n**Status:** escalated · **Run:** `wf_192cd4bd-629` · **Date:** 2026-06-03\n**Run-record:** `evals/run-records/pinewood-derby-sim/0003-web-front-end.json`\n\nThe build-loop ran the approved PRD/TRD, was interrupted by the recurring\n`subagent completed without calling StructuredOutput` crash (29 agents, ~2.15M output\ntokens, ~99 min), and on resume could **not** be brought to PO sign-off. Two distinct\nblockers — one a real defect for a human to adjudicate, one environmental — require a\ndecision before this feature can finish. Nothing was papered over: the failing tests are\nleft RED on disk, exactly as with 0001's AC-E4.\n\n## On-disk state (verified by the profile gate commands)\n\n- **`uv run pytest`** — 448 passed, **3 failed**, 1 skipped (452 collected; +136 vs 0001's 316).\n- **`uv run ruff check .`** — clean. · **`uv run mypy .` (strict)** — clean (50 files).\n- Built: `src/pinewood_derby/present.py` (507 lines, the folded 0002 translation layer) +\n  8 new test modules. **No `web/` workspace** (see Blocker 2).\n\nThe 3 RED tests all trace to **one** root cause (Blocker 1); the other two are\nfull-suite-subprocess meta-tests that cascade from it:\n- `tests/test_present.py::test_ac3_to_json_preserves_full_trajectory`\n- `tests/test_nfr_wi13.py::test_nfr_coverage_engine_and_overall_meet_bar`\n- `tests/test_engine_adversarial_wi7_adv_p2_001.py::test_wi7_adv_p2_001_full_suite_is_green_against_live_engine`\n\n## Blocker 1 — Two acceptance tests contradict each other (needs your ruling)\n\nWI01 (view-model) and WI04 (no-jargon guard) wrote acceptance tests that **cannot both be\ngreen**:\n\n- **WI01 / AC-R1** — `test_ac3_to_json_preserves_full_trajectory` asserts the JSON payload\n  the bridge ships contains a key literally named **`\"trajectory\"`** (so the animator can\n  replay the run): `assert \"trajectory\" in payload`.\n- **WI04 / AC-X3** — `test_to_json_payload_is_jargon_free_across_matrix` scans the payload\n  **including its dict keys** (`_iter_view_strings` recurses into keys) and asserts no\n  banned term appears. The WI04 banned-term list **includes `\"trajectory\"`** (and\n  `\"proportion\"`), and `test_exposed_banned_terms_cover_the_agreed_list` pins that list as a\n  required superset.\n\nSo a `\"trajectory\"` key satisfies WI01 and fails WI04; renaming it (the dev chose\n`\"frames\"`) satisfies WI04 and fails WI01. The developer correctly **refused to edit either\ntest** to force green (integrity rule) and looped on the impossible green gate until the\nStructuredOutput crash. This is a genuine requirements conflict, not a code bug — it needs a\nhuman ruling, and because the no-jargon guard is a **protective educational-accuracy gate**,\nI did not unilaterally weaken it.\n\n**Recommended resolution (for your approval — not yet applied):** AC-X3 governs *kid-facing\ntext — strings rendered to the user* — not internal JSON data keys the animator consumes.\nWI04 over-reached on two axes beyond the PRD's enumerated list (\"Joules, Newtons,\ncoefficient, m/s², C_d, μ, moment of inertia, normal force\"): (a) it scans dict **keys**, and\n(b) it added `\"trajectory\"`/`\"proportion\"`, which are not kid-facing units. The clean fix is\nto **narrow the WI04 payload scan to values** (the strings the kid actually sees) and drop\n`\"trajectory\"`/`\"proportion\"` from the banned-key set, then keep the `\"trajectory\"` key for\nthe animator (WI01). This preserves the guard's real purpose (no jargon in rendered copy)\nwhile letting the data layer name its fields plainly. *Alternative*, if you'd rather keep\nWI04 verbatim: rename the WI01 test's expected key to `\"frames\"` — but that bakes a jargon\nrule into a data contract and is the weaker choice. **Either way edits a protective/acceptance\ntest, so it's your call.**\n\n## Blocker 2 — The UI half cannot be built in this environment (no Node toolchain)\n\nThe PO decomposed 15 work items. WI07–WI14 are the TypeScript + Vite + `<canvas>` UI and the\nPyodide bridge, all verified via **Playwright headless-browser tests** (TRD §10/§12). This\nmachine has **no `node`/`npm`/`npx`** — only `uv`/Python — so those work items have no test\nrunner the profile's `uv run pytest` can drive, and **none were started**. This is the\n\"test-stack expansion beyond the profile's Python-only toolchain\" risk the TRD §10/§11 called\nout, compounded by the fact that the **0006 profile reconciliation** (desktop-app → web-app,\nadd the web `commands`/`framework`) has not run yet.\n\n**To proceed you must decide one of:**\n1. Install a Node/Vite/Playwright toolchain (and land 0006 to update the profile's\n   `commands`/`framework`/`archetype`), then resume the build for WI07–WI15; **or**\n2. Accept this feature as the **pure-Python translation layer only** (WI01–WI06 + WI15's\n   Python gate) and split the browser UI into its own feature once the toolchain + profile\n   are in place.\n\n## Work-item ledger\n\n| WI | Scope | State | Note |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| WI01 viewmodel | present()/to_json core | **escalated** | blocked by Blocker 1 (trajectory key) |\n| WI02 breakdown | \"where did your speed go?\" | passed | green, incl. adversarial |\n| WI03 why/priority | dominant-factor + tips | passed | green, 3 adversarial passes |\n| WI04 no-jargon | banned-terms guard | passed | green — but is the other half of Blocker 1 |\n| WI05 DNF classifier | tipped vs stalled | passed | classifier in present.py; R4 tests green |\n| WI06 garage serde | to_dict/from_dict | **abandoned** | not built (no `to_dict`/`from_dict`) |\n| WI07–WI14 | Pyodide bridge + TS/canvas UI + Playwright | **abandoned** | Blocker 2 (no Node) |\n| WI15 purity guard | no-physics-outside-engine | **abandoned** | ruff/mypy/0001-suite pass; dedicated guard test not written |\n\n## Metrics (run-record)\n\n15 work items decomposed · 7 adversarial review passes · 12 findings (2 critical, 4 high,\n3 medium, 3 low; 11 reproducible) · 0 PO rejections (sign-off never reached) ·\nacceptance_first_pass = false · escalations = 1.\n\n## Signals for the eval-loop / synthesizer\n\n1. **`StructuredOutput` crash recurs** on long sessions — now 6× across 0001+0003 (the dev\n   `devToGreen` retry loop here). A known measurement/robustness gap.\n2. **The green gate runs the whole suite**, so a later WI's change can turn an earlier WI's\n   accepted test RED — here WI04's banned-key choice broke WI01's trajectory test. The\n   build-loop has no cross-WI acceptance-test **consistency check** before a WI is accepted;\n   two WIs can ship mutually contradictory tests and only collide at the green gate.\n3. **Profile/toolchain drift is unenforced.** The build-loop launched a web-frontend feature\n   against a Python-only profile whose `commands` can't run the UI tests. A pre-flight gate\n   that checks the feature's required toolchain against the profile (or requires the\n   profile-reconciliation feature to land first) would have caught Blocker 2 before spending\n   ~2.15M tokens. 0006 (profile reconciliation) is the prerequisite this feature needed.\n4. **Adversarial-reviewer scope** again surfaced findings tied to non-finish presentation —\n   consistent with the 0001 WI12-ADV-006 lineage that created AC-R4.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":393,"cache_read_input_tokens":141287,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":393},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55f4d0f9-3f78-404c-9d9b-b1c51c035e71","uuid":"bbf1e2e9-2f4d-442d-b3d6-1de4f3942321","request_id":"req_011CbgMWNfGR7NdxZgJVJzjo"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QAtnMA7MMW5UckYbbcYGe6","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/ericburdett/Projects/agentic-sdlc/apps/pinewood-derby-sim/features/0003-web-front-end/ESCALATION.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55f4d0f9-3f78-404c-9d9b-b1c51c035e71","uuid":"53392ae0-7b2e-4317-849f-c7e5bb557e55","timestamp":"2026-06-03T12:50:22.179Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/ericburdett/Projects/agentic-sdlc/apps/pinewood-derby-sim/features/0003-web-front-end/ESCALATION.md","content":"# 0003-web-front-end — ESCALATION\n\n**Status:** escalated · **Run:** `wf_192cd4bd-629` · **Date:** 2026-06-03\n**Run-record:** `evals/run-records/pinewood-derby-sim/0003-web-front-end.json`\n\nThe build-loop ran the approved PRD/TRD, was interrupted by the recurring\n`subagent completed without calling StructuredOutput` crash (29 agents, ~2.15M output\ntokens, ~99 min), and on resume could **not** be brought to PO sign-off. Two distinct\nblockers — one a real defect for a human to adjudicate, one environmental — require a\ndecision before this feature can finish. Nothing was papered over: the failing tests are\nleft RED on disk, exactly as with 0001's AC-E4.\n\n## On-disk state (verified by the profile gate commands)\n\n- **`uv run pytest`** — 448 passed, **3 failed**, 1 skipped (452 collected; +136 vs 0001's 316).\n- **`uv run ruff check .`** — clean. · **`uv run mypy .` (strict)** — clean (50 files).\n- Built: `src/pinewood_derby/present.py` (507 lines, the folded 0002 translation layer) +\n  8 new test modules. **No `web/` workspace** (see Blocker 2).\n\nThe 3 RED tests all trace to **one** root cause (Blocker 1); the other two are\nfull-suite-subprocess meta-tests that cascade from it:\n- `tests/test_present.py::test_ac3_to_json_preserves_full_trajectory`\n- `tests/test_nfr_wi13.py::test_nfr_coverage_engine_and_overall_meet_bar`\n- `tests/test_engine_adversarial_wi7_adv_p2_001.py::test_wi7_adv_p2_001_full_suite_is_green_against_live_engine`\n\n## Blocker 1 — Two acceptance tests contradict each other (needs your ruling)\n\nWI01 (view-model) and WI04 (no-jargon guard) wrote acceptance tests that **cannot both be\ngreen**:\n\n- **WI01 / AC-R1** — `test_ac3_to_json_preserves_full_trajectory` asserts the JSON payload\n  the bridge ships contains a key literally named **`\"trajectory\"`** (so the animator can\n  replay the run): `assert \"trajectory\" in payload`.\n- **WI04 / AC-X3** — `test_to_json_payload_is_jargon_free_across_matrix` scans the payload\n  **including its dict keys** (`_iter_view_strings` recurses into keys) and asserts no\n  banned term appears. The WI04 banned-term list **includes `\"trajectory\"`** (and\n  `\"proportion\"`), and `test_exposed_banned_terms_cover_the_agreed_list` pins that list as a\n  required superset.\n\nSo a `\"trajectory\"` key satisfies WI01 and fails WI04; renaming it (the dev chose\n`\"frames\"`) satisfies WI04 and fails WI01. The developer correctly **refused to edit either\ntest** to force green (integrity rule) and looped on the impossible green gate until the\nStructuredOutput crash. This is a genuine requirements conflict, not a code bug — it needs a\nhuman ruling, and because the no-jargon guard is a **protective educational-accuracy gate**,\nI did not unilaterally weaken it.\n\n**Recommended resolution (for your approval — not yet applied):** AC-X3 governs *kid-facing\ntext — strings rendered to the user* — not internal JSON data keys the animator consumes.\nWI04 over-reached on two axes beyond the PRD's enumerated list (\"Joules, Newtons,\ncoefficient, m/s², C_d, μ, moment of inertia, normal force\"): (a) it scans dict **keys**, and\n(b) it added `\"trajectory\"`/`\"proportion\"`, which are not kid-facing units. The clean fix is\nto **narrow the WI04 payload scan to values** (the strings the kid actually sees) and drop\n`\"trajectory\"`/`\"proportion\"` from the banned-key set, then keep the `\"trajectory\"` key for\nthe animator (WI01). This preserves the guard's real purpose (no jargon in rendered copy)\nwhile letting the data layer name its fields plainly. *Alternative*, if you'd rather keep\nWI04 verbatim: rename the WI01 test's expected key to `\"frames\"` — but that bakes a jargon\nrule into a data contract and is the weaker choice. **Either way edits a protective/acceptance\ntest, so it's your call.**\n\n## Blocker 2 — The UI half cannot be built in this environment (no Node toolchain)\n\nThe PO decomposed 15 work items. WI07–WI14 are the TypeScript + Vite + `<canvas>` UI and the\nPyodide bridge, all verified via **Playwright headless-browser tests** (TRD §10/§12). This\nmachine has **no `node`/`npm`/`npx`** — only `uv`/Python — so those work items have no test\nrunner the profile's `uv run pytest` can drive, and **none were started**. This is the\n\"test-stack expansion beyond the profile's Python-only toolchain\" risk the TRD §10/§11 called\nout, compounded by the fact that the **0006 profile reconciliation** (desktop-app → web-app,\nadd the web `commands`/`framework`) has not run yet.\n\n**To proceed you must decide one of:**\n1. Install a Node/Vite/Playwright toolchain (and land 0006 to update the profile's\n   `commands`/`framework`/`archetype`), then resume the build for WI07–WI15; **or**\n2. Accept this feature as the **pure-Python translation layer only** (WI01–WI06 + WI15's\n   Python gate) and split the browser UI into its own feature once the toolchain + profile\n   are in place.\n\n## Work-item ledger\n\n| WI | Scope | State | Note |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| WI01 viewmodel | present()/to_json core | **escalated** | blocked by Blocker 1 (trajectory key) |\n| WI02 breakdown | \"where did your speed go?\" | passed | green, incl. adversarial |\n| WI03 why/priority | dominant-factor + tips | passed | green, 3 adversarial passes |\n| WI04 no-jargon | banned-terms guard | passed | green — but is the other half of Blocker 1 |\n| WI05 DNF classifier | tipped vs stalled | passed | classifier in present.py; R4 tests green |\n| WI06 garage serde | to_dict/from_dict | **abandoned** | not built (no `to_dict`/`from_dict`) |\n| WI07–WI14 | Pyodide bridge + TS/canvas UI + Playwright | **abandoned** | Blocker 2 (no Node) |\n| WI15 purity guard | no-physics-outside-engine | **abandoned** | ruff/mypy/0001-suite pass; dedicated guard test not written |\n\n## Metrics (run-record)\n\n15 work items decomposed · 7 adversarial review passes · 12 findings (2 critical, 4 high,\n3 medium, 3 low; 11 reproducible) · 0 PO rejections (sign-off never reached) ·\nacceptance_first_pass = false · escalations = 1.\n\n## Signals for the eval-loop / synthesizer\n\n1. **`StructuredOutput` crash recurs** on long sessions — now 6× across 0001+0003 (the dev\n   `devToGreen` retry loop here). A known measurement/robustness gap.\n2. **The green gate runs the whole suite**, so a later WI's change can turn an earlier WI's\n   accepted test RED — here WI04's banned-key choice broke WI01's trajectory test. The\n   build-loop has no cross-WI acceptance-test **consistency check** before a WI is accepted;\n   two WIs can ship mutually contradictory tests and only collide at the green gate.\n3. **Profile/toolchain drift is unenforced.** The build-loop launched a web-frontend feature\n   against a Python-only profile whose `commands` can't run the UI tests. A pre-flight gate\n   that checks the feature's required toolchain against the profile (or requires the\n   profile-reconciliation feature to land first) would have caught Blocker 2 before spending\n   ~2.15M tokens. 0006 (profile reconciliation) is the prerequisite this feature needed.\n4. **Adversarial-reviewer scope** again surfaced findings tied to non-finish presentation —\n   consistent with the 0001 WI12-ADV-006 lineage that created AC-R4.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
